WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:04.760
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

2
00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:06.060
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

3
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:07.340
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》。

4
00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:08.600
And we're best friends.
我们是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:12.420
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.
现在，我们专门为你制作了终极版《办公室》重温播客。

6
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:19.400
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
每周，我们都会深度解析一集《办公室》，并分享只有身临其境的我们才能告诉你的独家幕后故事。

7
00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:20.560
We're The Office ladies.
我们是《办公室》女士。

8
00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:26.930
Okay, hi.
好的，嗨。

9
00:00:29.350 --> 00:00:30.450
It's Ed, hi.
是埃德，嗨。

10
00:00:30.590 --> 00:00:31.710
Surprise, you guys.
给你们个惊喜。

11
00:00:31.870 --> 00:00:36.430
We have Ed Helms here today, and we will be talking about Andy's play.
今天埃德·赫尔姆斯来到了现场，我们将聊聊安迪的戏剧。

12
00:00:36.430 --> 00:00:41.730
I didn't know if I was supposed to talk right away or if you were going to introduce me, but then you both looked at me.
我不知道是该马上说话，还是等你们介绍我，但你们俩都盯着我看。

13
00:00:41.730 --> 00:00:43.730
We just stared at you until you spoke.
我们只是盯着你看，直到你开口说话。

14
00:00:44.030 --> 00:00:45.250
Okay, so yeah, I'm talking.
好吧，没错，我在说话了。

15
00:00:45.370 --> 00:00:45.870
Now I'm talking.
现在我在说话了。

16
00:00:46.030 --> 00:00:46.390
I'm here.
我在这儿。

17
00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:50.570
Well, this is Season 7, Episode 3.
嗯，这是第七季第三集。

18
00:00:50.770 --> 00:00:54.490
It was written by Charlie Grandy, directed by John Scott.
由查理·格兰迪编剧，约翰·斯科特执导。

19
00:00:54.910 --> 00:00:55.810
Would you like a summary?
需要剧情梗概吗？

20
00:00:56.310 --> 00:00:57.510
I mean, I would love that one more.
我是说，我非常乐意听听。

21
00:00:57.630 --> 00:00:58.790
Ed, what do you think about a summary?
埃德，你觉得要不要来个梗概？

22
00:00:58.890 --> 00:00:59.250
Feeling good?
感觉如何？

23
00:00:59.310 --> 00:00:59.870
I love summaries.
我喜欢梗概。

24
00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:00.610
I love a summary.
我喜欢梗概。

25
00:01:00.810 --> 00:01:01.370
Here it is.
梗概如下。

26
00:01:01.370 --> 00:01:10.850
Andy invites his co-workers to watch him in a community theater production of Sweeney Todd, which Michael is upset to learn he was not cast in.
安迪邀请同事们去看他参演的社区剧院版《理发师陶德》，迈克尔得知自己没被选上后很不高兴。

27
00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:16.790
The entire office attends, except for Aaron, who steps in at the last minute to babysit for Cece.
整个办公室的人都去了，除了亚伦，他临时顶替去照顾西西了。

28
00:01:17.730 --> 00:01:25.910
And Angela is going to get another punch on her punch card from Dwight, but not for the reason, you might think.
安吉拉又要从德怀特那里获得一张打孔卡上的印章了，但原因可能和你想象的不一样。

29
00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:27.390
There it is.
就是这样。

30
00:01:27.490 --> 00:01:27.950
What do we think?
大家觉得怎么样？

31
00:01:28.150 --> 00:01:29.830
I thought that was a fantastic summary.
我觉得这个梗概棒极了。

32
00:01:29.850 --> 00:01:30.710
It's actually, yeah.
确实，没错。

33
00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:37.650
I re-watched the episode in preparation for this, and that summary is spot on.
为了准备这次节目，我重温了这一集，这个梗概非常精准。

34
00:01:37.790 --> 00:01:39.250
Oh, thank you.
哦，谢谢。

35
00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:39.790
Yeah.
没错。

36
00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:41.730
I wrote it myself.
我自己写的。

37
00:01:42.830 --> 00:01:51.050
I also thought maybe we want a quick summary of Sweeney Todd, the production that Andy is starring in, to give some context.
我还想也许我们需要一个《理发师陶德》的简要梗概，也就是安迪主演的那部戏，好提供一些背景信息。

38
00:01:51.310 --> 00:01:52.070
What do you guys think?
你们觉得呢？

39
00:01:52.390 --> 00:01:53.890
I want to hear it.
我想听听。

40
00:01:53.890 --> 00:01:57.470
I went down the Wikipedia rabbit hole about Sweeney Todd, and wow.
我钻进维基百科关于《理发师陶德》的词条里查了个底朝天，哇。

41
00:01:57.850 --> 00:01:58.210
Oh.
哦。

42
00:01:58.650 --> 00:01:59.890
Well, I hope I cover it.
好吧，希望我能讲清楚。

43
00:01:59.930 --> 00:02:01.290
If I don't, will you let me know?
如果我没讲清楚，你们会告诉我吗？

44
00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:01.890
Maybe.
也许吧。

45
00:02:02.250 --> 00:02:02.830
Oh, no.
哦，不。

46
00:02:02.890 --> 00:02:04.490
I didn't commit any of it to memory.
我没记住任何内容。

47
00:02:04.630 --> 00:02:05.630
There's just a lot of versions.
版本实在是太多了。

48
00:02:05.930 --> 00:02:12.370
I don't know anything about it, so I won't know if – I mean, I know what is in the episode, basically.
我对它一无所知，所以我也没法判断——我是说，我基本上只知道剧集里演了什么。

49
00:02:12.710 --> 00:02:13.070
Okay.
好吧。

50
00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:14.050
But I don't know the –
但我不知道——

51
00:02:14.050 --> 00:02:14.530
The musical.
音乐剧。

52
00:02:14.570 --> 00:02:19.510
And I know the premise, but I don't know the story, so anything you say is going to be fine with me.
我知道大概的背景，但不知道具体的故事，所以你说什么我都能接受。

53
00:02:19.770 --> 00:02:20.190
All right.
好吧。

54
00:02:20.330 --> 00:02:20.990
Well, here we go.
那么，我们开始吧。

55
00:02:20.990 --> 00:02:28.050
So, Sweeney Todd, The Demon Barber of Fleet Street is a real musical that first opened on Broadway in 1979.
《理发师陶德：舰队街的恶魔理发师》是一部真正的音乐剧，于1979年在百老汇首演。

56
00:02:28.670 --> 00:02:32.930
The music and lyrics are by Stephen Sondheim, and the book is by Hugh Wheeler.
词曲由斯蒂芬·桑德海姆创作，剧本由休·惠勒编写。

57
00:02:33.270 --> 00:02:43.530
The character of Sweeney Todd, a murderous barber who goes around killing people, it originated in Victorian serialized fiction known as The Penny Dreadfuls.
理发师陶德这个角色，是一个四处杀人的理发师，他起源于维多利亚时代的连载小说，也就是所谓的“便士惊悚小说”。

58
00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:43.930
Yes.
是的。

59
00:02:44.210 --> 00:02:45.850
I saw that on Wikipedia.
我在维基百科上看到了。

60
00:02:46.230 --> 00:02:48.710
I have one little beef with your summary, actually.
其实，我对你的总结有一点小意见。

61
00:02:48.810 --> 00:02:49.230
Are you done?
你说完了吗？

62
00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:49.690
You're not done.
你还没说完。

63
00:02:49.810 --> 00:02:51.150
I have a little more to say.
我还有点话要说。

64
00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:51.370
Okay.
好的。

65
00:02:51.390 --> 00:02:51.830
Okay, go for it.
行，你说吧。

66
00:02:51.910 --> 00:02:52.190
Okay.
好的。

67
00:02:52.430 --> 00:02:52.610
Sorry.
抱歉。

68
00:02:52.970 --> 00:02:55.510
Now, already one beef I've earned.
现在，我已经有一个意见了。

69
00:02:55.730 --> 00:02:55.950
No.
不。

70
00:02:56.170 --> 00:02:56.610
All right.
好吧。

71
00:02:56.770 --> 00:03:04.650
The musical was based on a play by Christopher Bond where he introduced a psychological backstory for Todd's crimes.
这部音乐剧改编自克里斯托弗·邦德的戏剧，他在剧中为陶德的罪行引入了心理学背景故事。

72
00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:10.330
And Stephen Sondheim had seen this play, and that inspired him to write the musical.
斯蒂芬·桑德海姆看了这部戏，这激发了他创作这部音乐剧的灵感。

73
00:03:10.930 --> 00:03:17.710
Over 80% of Sweeney Todd is set to music, either through singing or an underscore to dialogue.
《理发师陶德》中超过80%的内容都是配乐的，要么通过演唱，要么作为对白的背景音乐。

74
00:03:18.370 --> 00:03:23.770
And the musical won both the Tony and the Olivier Award for Best New Musical when it came out.
这部音乐剧在推出时同时获得了托尼奖和奥利弗奖的最佳新音乐剧奖。

75
00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:25.630
When was that that it came out?
它是什么时候推出的？

76
00:03:26.170 --> 00:03:26.610
1979.
1979年。

77
00:03:27.050 --> 00:03:27.570
Oh, right.
哦，对。

78
00:03:27.570 --> 00:03:28.350
What's your beef, Ed?
你有什么意见，埃德？

79
00:03:28.530 --> 00:03:31.370
Okay, so you said that he goes around killing people.
好的，你刚才说他四处杀人。

80
00:03:31.730 --> 00:03:35.550
He actually is a barber, and he murders people in his barbershop.
他其实是个理发师，他在自己的理发店里谋杀顾客。

81
00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:39.410
So, really, people come around to be murdered.
所以，实际上是人们自己送上门来被杀的。

82
00:03:39.530 --> 00:03:39.970
Exactly.
没错。

83
00:03:40.130 --> 00:03:40.310
Yes.
是的。

84
00:03:40.390 --> 00:03:41.510
That would have been more accurate.
那样说会更准确。

85
00:03:41.650 --> 00:03:42.990
He doesn't go around murdering.
他并不是四处去杀人。

86
00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:45.430
People come around to get murdered.
是人们自己找上门来被杀的。

87
00:03:45.970 --> 00:03:46.790
More accurate.
更准确。

88
00:03:46.990 --> 00:03:48.030
They come around for a haircut.
他们是来理发的。

89
00:03:48.510 --> 00:03:49.570
They come around for a haircut, yeah.
他们是来理发的，没错。

90
00:03:49.570 --> 00:03:51.270
And then he kills them with the straight razor.
然后他用直剃刀杀了他们。

91
00:03:51.430 --> 00:03:51.570
Right.
对。

92
00:03:51.690 --> 00:03:53.050
And then he opens the chair.
接着他打开椅子。

93
00:03:53.050 --> 00:03:56.290
He has a lever, and they go flying down into the basement.
他有个操纵杆，他们就会飞进地下室。

94
00:03:56.610 --> 00:04:02.250
And then he has a friend who turns their bodies into meat for really bad mince pies.
然后他有个朋友，会把他们的尸体做成肉馅，做成非常难吃的肉馅饼。

95
00:04:02.850 --> 00:04:03.850
Aren't they really yummy?
它们不是很好吃吗？

96
00:04:04.270 --> 00:04:04.830
Oh, yeah.
哦，是啊。

97
00:04:04.910 --> 00:04:05.130
Sorry.
抱歉。

98
00:04:05.250 --> 00:04:07.710
She has a song at the beginning that she has really bad pies.
她在一开始有首歌，唱的就是她的馅饼做得有多难吃。

99
00:04:07.930 --> 00:04:08.110
Oh.
哦。

100
00:04:08.410 --> 00:04:10.430
When the pies are people, then they're good?
当馅饼是用人肉做的时候，它们就好吃了？

101
00:04:10.610 --> 00:04:12.290
Yeah, then people can't get enough of the pies.
对，然后大家就对这些馅饼爱不释手了。

102
00:04:12.290 --> 00:04:13.030
Oh, my God.
天哪。

103
00:04:13.030 --> 00:04:15.250
I did not realize this part of the story.
我之前没意识到故事还有这一出。

104
00:04:15.350 --> 00:04:15.810
Oh, yeah.
噢，是啊。

105
00:04:16.030 --> 00:04:16.510
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

106
00:04:16.630 --> 00:04:17.650
There's a whole cannibalism.
里面居然还有吃人的情节。

107
00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:19.490
I mean, it's like accidental cannibalism.
我是说，那就像是意外吃人一样。

108
00:04:19.570 --> 00:04:21.510
They sell them as mince pies.
他们把那些馅饼当成肉馅饼卖。

109
00:04:21.610 --> 00:04:21.910
Yeah.
是啊。

110
00:04:21.990 --> 00:04:22.850
But they're people.
但那可是人肉啊。

111
00:04:22.850 --> 00:04:23.790
It's like Soylent Green.
就像《超世纪谍杀案》那样。

112
00:04:24.010 --> 00:04:24.270
Yeah.
没错。

113
00:04:24.390 --> 00:04:24.730
It's people.
是人肉。

114
00:04:24.970 --> 00:04:25.090
Yeah.
对。

115
00:04:25.250 --> 00:04:26.130
It's people, people.
是人肉，伙计们。

116
00:04:26.450 --> 00:04:26.770
It's people.
是人肉。

117
00:04:26.830 --> 00:04:27.370
Come on, people.
拜托，各位。

118
00:04:27.830 --> 00:04:28.190
Yeah.
是啊。

119
00:04:28.390 --> 00:04:28.950
People pies.
人肉馅饼。

120
00:04:29.530 --> 00:04:29.930
People pies.
人肉馅饼。

121
00:04:29.950 --> 00:04:30.050
Wow.
哇。

122
00:04:30.210 --> 00:04:32.210
The musical could have been called People Pies.
这部音乐剧本可以叫《人肉馅饼》的。

123
00:04:32.390 --> 00:04:32.990
It should have been.
确实应该叫这个。

124
00:04:33.130 --> 00:04:33.870
It should have been, really.
真的应该叫这个。

125
00:04:36.210 --> 00:04:37.210
I'm going to, yeah.
我会的，没错。

126
00:04:37.330 --> 00:04:39.170
We've got to write Stephen Sondheim a letter.
我们得给斯蒂芬·桑德海姆写封信。

127
00:04:39.350 --> 00:04:39.510
Yeah.
好。

128
00:04:39.510 --> 00:04:41.870
I'm getting out my old timey type of letter.
我这就拿出我那老式的信纸。

129
00:04:43.330 --> 00:04:47.130
Well, Ed, we can't wait to talk to you about this episode and your experience.
好了，埃德，我们迫不及待想和你聊聊这一集以及你的经历了。

130
00:04:47.470 --> 00:04:51.730
We thought we'd start by asking you, do you have any musical theater background?
我们想先问问你，你有音乐剧背景吗？

131
00:04:52.070 --> 00:04:52.350
Yeah.
有啊。

132
00:04:52.350 --> 00:04:53.490
Have you ever been in musicals?
你演过音乐剧吗？

133
00:04:53.550 --> 00:04:54.270
Like in high school?
比如高中时期？

134
00:04:54.510 --> 00:04:55.170
Well, yeah.
嗯，有。

135
00:04:55.170 --> 00:04:59.910
So I was in some musical theater productions in high school.
我在高中时确实参加过一些音乐剧演出。

136
00:05:00.490 --> 00:05:05.390
And then I was in, let's see, I was in Joseph and the Amazing Technicolor Dreamcoat.
然后我参加过，让我想想，我演过《约瑟夫与神奇彩衣》。

137
00:05:05.690 --> 00:05:05.930
Okay.
好的。

138
00:05:06.090 --> 00:05:07.250
Oh, Jenna and I both have one.
噢，珍娜和我都有过。

139
00:05:07.250 --> 00:05:08.550
And we're wondering if you were in.
我们想知道你演过什么。

140
00:05:08.650 --> 00:05:09.030
Keep going.
继续说。

141
00:05:10.490 --> 00:05:11.870
And gosh, I'm drawing a blank.
天哪，我脑子一片空白。

142
00:05:11.990 --> 00:05:13.790
Oh, I was in Into the Woods, another Sondheim.
噢，我还演过《拜访森林》，又是桑德海姆的作品。

143
00:05:13.790 --> 00:05:14.430
Oh, yes.
噢，没错。

144
00:05:14.550 --> 00:05:14.930
Into the Woods.
《拜访森林》。

145
00:05:14.990 --> 00:05:16.410
Another Sondheim masterpiece.
桑德海姆的另一部杰作。

146
00:05:17.890 --> 00:05:19.190
And that was all high school.
那些都是高中时候的事了。

147
00:05:19.350 --> 00:05:25.970
And then when I was in college, I did, I was in a musical called The Cradle Will Rock,
后来上大学时，我演过一部叫《摇篮将摇》的音乐剧，

148
00:05:26.330 --> 00:05:33.590
which is a really cool, like during the Great Depression, it was written as like a sort of pro worker.
那部剧真的很酷，背景是大萧条时期，写的是那种支持工人的题材。

149
00:05:34.250 --> 00:05:35.550
Anyway, it was a cool piece.
总之，那是一部很棒的作品。

150
00:05:35.550 --> 00:05:37.470
And that's what I did in college.
这就是我在大学时做的事情。

151
00:05:37.590 --> 00:05:38.410
And then I think that's it.
我想大概就是这样了。

152
00:05:39.190 --> 00:05:39.330
Wow.
哇。

153
00:05:39.630 --> 00:05:40.770
No Guys and Dolls, Jenna.
不是《红男绿女》，珍娜。

154
00:05:40.910 --> 00:05:42.610
We really were positive.
我们当时真的很确定。

155
00:05:42.610 --> 00:05:44.890
Really feeling like that'd be a good role for you.
觉得那角色真的很适合你。

156
00:05:45.250 --> 00:05:46.050
Nathan Detroit.
内森·底特律。

157
00:05:46.210 --> 00:05:46.410
Yeah.
是啊。

158
00:05:46.510 --> 00:05:46.630
Sure.
当然。

159
00:05:46.870 --> 00:05:47.430
Guys and Dolls.
《红男绿女》。

160
00:05:47.470 --> 00:05:48.370
Sit down, sit down, sit down, sit down.
坐下，坐下，坐下，坐下。

161
00:05:48.750 --> 00:05:48.990
Yeah.
是啊。

162
00:05:49.030 --> 00:05:49.570
Sit down, yeah, right.
坐下，对，没错。

163
00:05:50.290 --> 00:05:54.010
I don't, I'm not that, I don't know Guys and Dolls.
我不是，我没那么，我不了解《红男绿女》。

164
00:05:54.630 --> 00:05:57.850
And I wasn't in it, but I wish I was.
我没演过，但我希望我演过。

165
00:05:58.090 --> 00:05:59.630
Because then we'd have a lot more to talk about.
那样我们就有更多共同话题了。

166
00:06:02.290 --> 00:06:03.950
Did you do musical theater, Angela?
安吉拉，你演过音乐剧吗？

167
00:06:03.950 --> 00:06:09.010
Oh, I mean, I was in The Music Man at my school in Indonesia.
噢，我是说，我在印度尼西亚上学时演过《音乐人》。

168
00:06:09.490 --> 00:06:09.610
Awesome.
太棒了。

169
00:06:09.810 --> 00:06:10.050
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

170
00:06:10.210 --> 00:06:11.670
I played Amaryllis.
我演的是阿玛丽莉丝。

171
00:06:12.250 --> 00:06:16.710
And we thought it was really funny we would give everyone a nickname based off their character names.
我们当时觉得很有趣，就根据大家的角色名给每个人起了绰号。

172
00:06:16.730 --> 00:06:18.790
So everyone called me Amaryllis.
所以大家都叫我阿玛丽莉丝。

173
00:06:19.130 --> 00:06:19.550
Oh.
噢。

174
00:06:19.810 --> 00:06:19.990
Yeah.
是啊。

175
00:06:19.990 --> 00:06:24.470
So you, your life has just been a series of nicknames.
所以你，你的人生就是一连串的绰号。

176
00:06:24.690 --> 00:06:26.090
People love nicknaming you.
人们很喜欢给你起绰号。

177
00:06:26.270 --> 00:06:26.330
I know.
我知道。

178
00:06:27.090 --> 00:06:27.570
Hambone.
火腿骨。

179
00:06:28.270 --> 00:06:29.390
I'm a real ass.
我真是个混蛋。

180
00:06:30.310 --> 00:06:32.610
That was my big musical theater debut.
那就是我的音乐剧处女秀。

181
00:06:32.730 --> 00:06:35.170
But I actually get really anxious singing in front of people.
但我其实在别人面前唱歌会非常焦虑。

182
00:06:35.770 --> 00:06:40.350
I can be on stage doing, you know, zany comedy skits and things like that.
我可以在舞台上表演，你知道，演些滑稽的喜剧短剧之类的。

183
00:06:40.490 --> 00:06:42.430
But to sing in front of people makes me so anxious.
但在别人面前唱歌让我感到非常焦虑。

184
00:06:42.430 --> 00:06:46.930
So I opted then to go into the more serious theater productions.
所以我当时选择了去演更严肃的戏剧作品。

185
00:06:47.390 --> 00:06:48.190
Of course.
当然。

186
00:06:48.430 --> 00:06:48.910
I see.
我明白了。

187
00:06:49.410 --> 00:06:50.250
What about you?
你呢？

188
00:06:50.890 --> 00:06:52.890
I did in high school.
我高中时演过。

189
00:06:53.670 --> 00:06:55.390
I'm not a strong singer.
我唱歌不太行。

190
00:06:55.450 --> 00:06:57.270
So I was in the dance chorus.
所以我是在舞蹈合唱团。

191
00:06:57.550 --> 00:06:58.410
I've heard you sing.
我听过你唱歌。

192
00:06:58.550 --> 00:06:59.610
I think you have a great voice.
我觉得你的嗓音很棒。

193
00:06:59.890 --> 00:07:00.950
Thank you for saying that.
谢谢你这么说。

194
00:07:01.050 --> 00:07:02.370
I'm really self-conscious about it.
我对此真的很没自信。

195
00:07:02.470 --> 00:07:02.630
Oh.
噢。

196
00:07:03.030 --> 00:07:04.190
Well, I think.
嗯，我觉得。

197
00:07:04.330 --> 00:07:05.750
Anyway, I think you have a great voice.
总之，我觉得你的嗓音很棒。

198
00:07:05.890 --> 00:07:06.550
So you danced.
所以你跳舞了。

199
00:07:06.670 --> 00:07:07.290
You were in the chorus.
你在合唱团里。

200
00:07:07.290 --> 00:07:08.530
I did the dancing chorus.
我参加了舞蹈合唱团。

201
00:07:08.530 --> 00:07:13.930
And then my senior year, I got the lead dance role in Fiddler on the Roof.
大四那年，我在《屋顶上的提琴手》里拿到了领舞的角色。

202
00:07:13.950 --> 00:07:14.830
I was the Fiddler.
我演的是那个提琴手。

203
00:07:14.970 --> 00:07:15.310
Wow.
哇。

204
00:07:16.230 --> 00:07:19.150
To which I say, without me, it was just called The Roof.
对此我想说，要是没我，那剧名就只剩《屋顶》了。

205
00:07:19.470 --> 00:07:19.870
Wow.
哇。

206
00:07:19.990 --> 00:07:20.310
Yeah, of course.
是啊，当然。

207
00:07:20.310 --> 00:07:21.550
You really, it's an important role.
你真的，那是个很重要的角色。

208
00:07:21.630 --> 00:07:23.250
I had no lines and didn't sing.
我没有台词，也不用唱歌。

209
00:07:23.410 --> 00:07:25.850
But I danced my heart out and I pretended to fiddle.
但我跳得非常卖力，还假装在拉琴。

210
00:07:26.030 --> 00:07:26.350
Yeah.
是啊。

211
00:07:26.950 --> 00:07:27.590
That's awesome.
太棒了。

212
00:07:27.690 --> 00:07:29.450
I just remembered another one that I was in.
我刚又想起一部我演过的剧。

213
00:07:29.610 --> 00:07:29.870
What?
什么？

214
00:07:30.390 --> 00:07:30.790
Godspell.
《福音》。

215
00:07:31.150 --> 00:07:33.110
Oh, I was in Godspell in college.
哦，我在大学时也演过《福音》。

216
00:07:33.230 --> 00:07:33.550
Hey.
嘿。

217
00:07:33.810 --> 00:07:34.250
High five.
击个掌。

218
00:07:34.350 --> 00:07:34.830
High five.
击个掌。

219
00:07:35.110 --> 00:07:35.370
Yeah.
好。

220
00:07:35.370 --> 00:07:38.070
And then, oh, and in college, I was in.
还有，哦，大学里我还演过。

221
00:07:38.450 --> 00:07:39.230
It's all dancing.
全是舞蹈。

222
00:07:39.390 --> 00:07:39.950
Bob Fosse.
鲍勃·福斯。

223
00:07:40.290 --> 00:07:41.070
Oh, Chicago?
哦，《芝加哥》？

224
00:07:41.350 --> 00:07:41.510
Oh, Horse Line?
哦，《歌舞线上》？

225
00:07:41.990 --> 00:07:42.430
No.
不是。

226
00:07:43.350 --> 00:07:44.090
The one.
那一部。

227
00:07:44.730 --> 00:07:47.010
Nice job, us just pulling out some Fosse.
干得漂亮，我们居然能想出福斯的作品。

228
00:07:47.330 --> 00:07:48.130
Liza Minnelli.
丽莎·明内利。

229
00:07:50.250 --> 00:07:50.690
Cabaret?
《歌厅》？

230
00:07:51.010 --> 00:07:51.550
That's it.
就是它。

231
00:07:51.630 --> 00:07:52.110
Thank you, Devin.
谢谢你，德文。

232
00:07:52.110 --> 00:07:52.570
Thank you, Devin.
谢谢你，德文。

233
00:07:52.750 --> 00:07:53.670
I was going to say Arthur.
我本来想说《亚瑟》的。

234
00:07:53.890 --> 00:07:54.150
No.
不是。

235
00:07:55.970 --> 00:07:56.410
Yes.
是的。

236
00:07:56.410 --> 00:07:59.490
And also in college, I was in cabaret and I got to choreograph that.
而且大学时我还演了《歌厅》，我还负责了编舞。

237
00:07:59.730 --> 00:08:02.770
So very like dance forward musicals were my thing.
所以那种以舞蹈为主的音乐剧是我的强项。

238
00:08:03.110 --> 00:08:04.210
I'm very impressed.
我印象深刻。

239
00:08:04.390 --> 00:08:04.870
Thank you.
谢谢。

240
00:08:05.370 --> 00:08:05.690
Okay.
好的。

241
00:08:05.890 --> 00:08:09.150
So we are here to talk about Andy performing Sweeney Todd.
我们今天是为了聊安迪表演《理发师陶德》而来的。

242
00:08:10.090 --> 00:08:10.890
Randy Cordray.
兰迪·科德雷。

243
00:08:11.110 --> 00:08:12.630
We talk to Randy Cordray all the time.
我们经常和兰迪·科德雷交流。

244
00:08:12.770 --> 00:08:13.290
He's amazing.
他太棒了。

245
00:08:13.610 --> 00:08:18.630
He told us the writers originally pitched the storyline over the summer between seasons
他告诉我们，编剧最初是在第六季和第七季之间的那个夏天提出这个剧情线的。

246
00:08:18.630 --> 00:08:19.610
six and seven.
你是怎么第一次听说这件事的？

247
00:08:20.210 --> 00:08:21.570
How did you first hear about it?
他们有没有来找你说，嘿，艾德，我们想做一部完整的音乐剧。

248
00:08:21.710 --> 00:08:24.490
Did they come to you and say, hey, Ed, we want to do a full musical.
你要唱很多歌。

249
00:08:24.690 --> 00:08:25.710
You're going to sing a bunch.
就是说，你有没有提出什么建议？

250
00:08:25.910 --> 00:08:26.750
Like, did you have any input?
就是说，你有没有提出什么建议？

251
00:08:27.290 --> 00:08:31.530
I don't recall knowing anything about it before the table read.
在剧本围读会之前，我不记得自己对这件事有任何了解。

252
00:08:31.530 --> 00:08:33.910
I'm shocked and also not shocked.
我感到震惊，但又不那么震惊。

253
00:08:34.050 --> 00:08:34.130
Not shocked.
不震惊。

254
00:08:34.130 --> 00:08:34.230
Yeah.
是啊。

255
00:08:34.310 --> 00:08:38.130
I mean, we were so buried in whatever episode we were working on.
我的意思是，我们当时正忙于手头正在制作的那一集。

256
00:08:38.250 --> 00:08:40.530
It's not like there was a lot of extra time.
我们并没有多少额外的时间。

257
00:08:40.690 --> 00:08:47.350
But now that you mention it, I'm sure that I must have started rehearsing before, like,
但既然你提到了，我肯定在那之前就开始排练了，大概是，

258
00:08:47.430 --> 00:08:48.790
at least the week before.
至少提前一周吧。

259
00:08:48.790 --> 00:08:49.790
Yeah.
是啊。

260
00:08:49.990 --> 00:08:51.490
Because that's hard music.
因为那音乐很难。

261
00:08:51.690 --> 00:08:54.430
Sondheim is, like, crazy hard music.
桑德海姆的音乐，简直难到离谱。

262
00:08:54.630 --> 00:08:54.810
Yeah.
是啊。

263
00:08:55.610 --> 00:08:55.830
Yeah.
没错。

264
00:08:56.110 --> 00:09:00.790
Randy told us that on his schedule, he went back and looked in his files.
兰迪告诉我们，他查了自己的日程表和档案。

265
00:09:00.790 --> 00:09:07.270
The only day that you guys had to rehearse all together as a cast was, like, the Monday
你们全员聚在一起排练的唯一一天，大概就是周一

266
00:09:07.270 --> 00:09:10.330
morning for half a day at the theater.
上午，在剧院排了半天。

267
00:09:10.790 --> 00:09:13.730
And then we all came and started shooting the episode.
然后我们就都到了，开始拍摄那一集。

268
00:09:14.010 --> 00:09:14.170
Yeah.
是啊。

269
00:09:14.170 --> 00:09:15.010
Does that sound right?
听起来对吗？

270
00:09:15.130 --> 00:09:15.950
That does sound right.
听起来确实没错。

271
00:09:15.950 --> 00:09:20.810
But if you, you know, if you're paying attention to the episode, there's not that much of the
但如果你注意看那一集的话，你会发现其实并没有出现太多

272
00:09:20.810 --> 00:09:21.850
play that you see.
剧里的内容。

273
00:09:22.090 --> 00:09:24.930
You know, like, it's not a ton of production time.
你知道，制作时间其实并不长。

274
00:09:25.350 --> 00:09:29.070
So I think we really only rehearsed a couple of things.
所以我认为我们真的只排练了几个片段。

275
00:09:29.250 --> 00:09:32.010
The much more complicated thing was the cold open.
更复杂的是片头那段戏。

276
00:09:32.130 --> 00:09:32.430
Yeah.
是啊。

277
00:09:32.550 --> 00:09:32.770
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

278
00:09:32.770 --> 00:09:35.770
And that, because that was a whole song that we all learned.
那是因为那是一整首歌，我们所有人都得学。

279
00:09:35.930 --> 00:09:37.130
And then there was choreography.
而且还有编舞。

280
00:09:37.890 --> 00:09:42.230
It looks, in the execution, it looks spontaneous, like we're just running around the space.
从呈现效果来看，它看起来很自然，就像我们只是在空间里跑来跑去一样。

281
00:09:42.330 --> 00:09:44.630
But obviously, it was all meticulously blocked.
但显然，所有的走位都是精心设计过的。

282
00:09:45.130 --> 00:09:51.870
And all of the fun, dramatic flourishes that everybody is doing in that scene, that I remember
每个人在那个场景里做的那些有趣、戏剧性的动作，我记得

283
00:09:51.870 --> 00:09:57.250
being quite complicated and learning that song was very hard.
当时非常复杂，学那首歌也很难。

284
00:09:57.470 --> 00:10:01.930
Because, again, Sondheim, he doesn't like to write melodies that you expect.
因为还是那句话，桑德海姆不喜欢写那种你预料之中的旋律。

285
00:10:02.330 --> 00:10:06.890
Everything kind of goes in weird directions and rhythms are weird.
一切都朝着奇怪的方向发展，节奏也很怪。

286
00:10:07.210 --> 00:10:15.170
It's like that ends with, like, the cadence is like the demon barber of Fleet Street or
就像结尾的那个节奏，就像《理发师陶德》或者

287
00:10:15.170 --> 00:10:18.850
something like, it's like a straight, you know, like a weird hiccup-y thing and everyone
类似的东西，它就是那种直白的、你知道的，那种奇怪的、断断续续的感觉，每个人

288
00:10:18.850 --> 00:10:19.510
had to get it right.
都必须把它唱准。

289
00:10:19.510 --> 00:10:25.550
But, yeah, there was, you were just saying earlier how you are nervous to sing in front
不过，说起来，你刚才还在说你在别人面前唱歌会紧张。

290
00:10:25.550 --> 00:10:26.030
of people.
显然，我非常喜欢唱歌。

291
00:10:27.030 --> 00:10:30.350
And I love to sing, obviously.
认识我的人都知道，我爱唱歌。

292
00:10:30.910 --> 00:10:33.130
Anyone who knows me, I love to sing.
但我其实记歌词很吃力。

293
00:10:33.230 --> 00:10:35.230
But I actually struggle with lyrics.
所以我真的很难记住歌词。

294
00:10:35.350 --> 00:10:38.450
And so I really have a hard time memorizing lyrics.
这会让我在这类表演场合感到非常焦虑，或者，你知道，

295
00:10:38.590 --> 00:10:44.210
And that can then make me really anxious in a performance setting or, like, you know,
如果我不得不，你知道，就像有几次我必须在《办公室》里唱长歌的时候，

296
00:10:44.270 --> 00:10:48.550
if I have to, you know, like there were a few times I had to sing, like, long songs on
那真的让我陷入恐慌状态。

297
00:10:48.550 --> 00:10:48.910
the office.
所以那一次，那个片头真的很难。

298
00:10:49.230 --> 00:10:52.190
And I, it just, yeah, it puts me in a panic state.
但我也不确定。

299
00:10:52.410 --> 00:10:54.470
So that one, that cold open was really hard.
所以那一次，那个片头真的很难。

300
00:10:55.190 --> 00:10:56.210
But I don't know.
但我也不确定。

301
00:10:56.330 --> 00:10:57.350
It was enough rehearsal time.
排练时间足够了。

302
00:10:57.830 --> 00:11:01.390
Were you singing live when you guys did that?
你们当时是现场演唱的吗？

303
00:11:01.390 --> 00:11:03.790
Or were you singing to, like, a playback recording?
还是说你们是跟着录音对口型？

304
00:11:03.950 --> 00:11:04.870
It seems live.
看起来像是现场唱的。

305
00:11:05.070 --> 00:11:05.570
It is.
确实是。

306
00:11:05.670 --> 00:11:06.410
It's all live.
全都是现场演唱。

307
00:11:06.570 --> 00:11:06.710
Yeah, that's my memory.
没错，我的记忆也是这样。

308
00:11:06.710 --> 00:11:08.430
And even the stuff in the theater is live.
甚至剧院里的那些表演也是现场的。

309
00:11:08.590 --> 00:11:09.390
I thought so.
我就觉得是。

310
00:11:09.410 --> 00:11:09.690
Yeah.
是的。

311
00:11:09.690 --> 00:11:11.170
That was my memory, too.
我的记忆也是这样。

312
00:11:11.410 --> 00:11:11.630
Yeah.
没错。

313
00:11:12.170 --> 00:11:12.410
Oh.
噢。

314
00:11:12.730 --> 00:11:16.050
The, the, the, the, the boombox is fake.
那个收音机是假的。

315
00:11:16.450 --> 00:11:18.650
Like, there was, you know, obviously that was.
就是，你知道，那显然是假的。

316
00:11:18.790 --> 00:11:19.310
That you hit.
你按了那个。

317
00:11:19.410 --> 00:11:20.650
I hit play on the boombox.
我按了收音机的播放键。

318
00:11:20.790 --> 00:11:25.290
And then, but I think they had a, they had a guide track sort of pumped in under the desks
不过我想他们应该在桌子底下放了引导音轨之类的东西，

319
00:11:25.290 --> 00:11:28.150
or something that we sang along to.
或者类似的东西让我们跟着唱。

320
00:11:28.290 --> 00:11:31.010
But, yeah, that was all real singing.
但没错，那确实都是真唱。

321
00:11:31.410 --> 00:11:35.770
I remember the first take we did of that cold open when you guys came in.
我记得你们进来时，我们拍那段开场戏的第一条。

322
00:11:35.770 --> 00:11:37.290
We did not know anything.
我们什么都不知道。

323
00:11:37.450 --> 00:11:39.110
We had not seen you rehearse.
我们没看过你们排练。

324
00:11:39.350 --> 00:11:40.870
It was a complete surprise.
完全是个惊喜。

325
00:11:41.330 --> 00:11:44.010
I found it so delightful and amazing.
我觉得那场面既令人愉悦又惊艳。

326
00:11:44.230 --> 00:11:48.430
It was also my first time seeing all of the costumes, which were so well done.
那也是我第一次看到所有的服装，做得真好。

327
00:11:48.550 --> 00:11:48.790
Yeah.
没错。

328
00:11:49.370 --> 00:11:50.790
And it was good.
而且效果很好。

329
00:11:50.950 --> 00:11:52.130
You guys were good.
你们表现得很好。

330
00:11:52.130 --> 00:11:54.610
And I didn't know if it would be good or bad.
我当时还不知道效果会好还是坏。

331
00:11:54.970 --> 00:12:00.190
And I heard that you actually fought for the production of Sweeney Todd to be good and not bad.
我听说你为了让《理发师陶德》的制作效果好而不是很烂，其实争取过。

332
00:12:00.350 --> 00:12:01.170
I did.
我确实争取过。

333
00:12:01.170 --> 00:12:08.470
Yeah, I was very passionate about that because I don't think that, I mean, there are exceptions,
是的，我对此非常执着，因为我不认为——我是说，虽然有例外，

334
00:12:08.750 --> 00:12:15.330
but I generally don't think that, like, intentionally bad performance for comedy works.
但我通常认为，为了喜剧效果而故意演得很烂是行不通的。

335
00:12:15.690 --> 00:12:18.390
It feels, like, cheap and easy and, like.
那样感觉很廉价、很敷衍，而且……

