00:18:41.370 --> 00:18:43.890
this, yeah, this is not, not good.
这，嗯，这不太好。

450
00:18:44.190 --> 00:18:44.630
Yeah.
没错。

451
00:18:44.970 --> 00:18:51.910
I loved Andy's earnestness when Aaron had to take the babysitting job when he's like, I get it.
我很喜欢安迪那种真诚的态度，尤其是亚伦不得不去当保姆的时候，他说他理解。

452
00:18:51.990 --> 00:18:53.130
It's a huge opportunity.
这是一个绝佳的机会。

453
00:18:53.530 --> 00:18:54.070
Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.
是啊，是啊，是啊，是啊。

454
00:18:56.530 --> 00:18:57.690
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

455
00:18:57.790 --> 00:18:59.890
He's checking his phone backstage.
他在后台看手机呢。

456
00:19:00.590 --> 00:19:02.150
One of the most brilliant.
最精彩的片段之一。

457
00:19:02.950 --> 00:19:09.610
Okay, so this is actually funny because I was saying before how I generally think that performing badly is a cheap joke.
好吧，这其实很有趣，因为我之前说过，我通常认为故意演砸是一种廉价的笑料。

458
00:19:09.610 --> 00:19:16.590
Like, if it's, if you're performing, you know, in a performance context and you're doing it badly on purpose.
比如，如果你是在表演，在表演的情境下，你故意演得很烂。

459
00:19:16.770 --> 00:19:20.570
I don't like that usually, but the tag of this episode.
我通常不喜欢那样，但这一集的结尾彩蛋。

460
00:19:20.670 --> 00:19:21.850
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

461
00:19:22.210 --> 00:19:23.170
Of Michael Scott doing.
迈克尔·斯科特演的。

462
00:19:23.630 --> 00:19:24.670
Law and order.
《法律与秩序》。

463
00:19:25.150 --> 00:19:26.210
An entire episode.
整整一集。

464
00:19:26.350 --> 00:19:27.290
So badly.
演得那么烂。

465
00:19:27.290 --> 00:19:27.830
As a monologue.
作为独白。

466
00:19:27.990 --> 00:19:28.530
So badly.
演得那么烂。

467
00:19:28.890 --> 00:19:31.130
It's so funny.
太搞笑了。

468
00:19:31.410 --> 00:19:34.070
I watched that four or five times.
我看了四五遍。

469
00:19:34.310 --> 00:19:36.250
It's just, it's priceless.
简直是无价之宝。

470
00:19:36.250 --> 00:19:40.610
But how many people could do that and sell it but Steve, you know?
但除了史蒂夫，还有谁能做到并演得这么传神呢，你懂的？

471
00:19:40.890 --> 00:19:43.030
Because that, I believed it.
因为那一刻，我相信了。

472
00:19:43.110 --> 00:19:46.170
I believed every second that that's how Michael Scott would have done it.
我百分之百相信迈克尔·斯科特就是会那样演。

473
00:19:46.230 --> 00:19:46.970
A hundred percent.
百分之百。

474
00:19:47.210 --> 00:19:51.750
And, you know, Steve almost never broke on, I mean, he very rarely broke.
而且，你知道，史蒂夫几乎从不笑场，我是说，他很少笑场。

475
00:19:51.810 --> 00:19:51.970
Right.
没错。

476
00:19:52.450 --> 00:19:55.690
And I was watching that being like, he had to be cracking himself up.
我当时看的时候就在想，他肯定憋笑憋得很辛苦。

477
00:19:55.870 --> 00:20:00.250
Like, this was, there were, I guarantee you, there were a few times he broke, you know.
我是说，我敢保证，他肯定有几次笑场了，你懂的。

478
00:20:00.250 --> 00:20:05.430
When he was slinging, I don't know, what, is it a belt or a sash or something as the lady?
当他挥舞着，我不知道，那是什么，腰带还是饰带之类的，扮演那个女士的时候？

479
00:20:05.570 --> 00:20:05.830
Yeah.
是啊。

480
00:20:05.970 --> 00:20:07.430
I know he broke doing that.
我知道他演那段时肯定笑场了。

481
00:20:07.530 --> 00:20:09.530
I know he had to have cracked himself up.
我知道他肯定把自己逗乐了。

482
00:20:09.570 --> 00:20:13.490
Or singing the theme song, like, da, da, da, da, da.
还有唱主题曲的时候，那种，哒，哒，哒，哒，哒。

483
00:20:14.330 --> 00:20:16.030
Just, oh, my God.
简直了，天哪。

484
00:20:16.170 --> 00:20:16.670
I know.
我知道。

485
00:20:16.910 --> 00:20:17.350
Priceless.
无价之宝。

486
00:20:18.150 --> 00:20:23.850
Do you guys, I'm curious, like, we made so many Office episodes.
你们呢，我很好奇，我们拍了那么多集《办公室》。

487
00:20:23.850 --> 00:20:33.290
And it's really funny to me the way fans understand the episodes as these, like, very tight, coherent stories.
粉丝们把这些剧集理解为非常紧凑、连贯的故事，这让我觉得很有趣。

488
00:20:34.590 --> 00:20:46.730
Whereas I find that from our perspective as the actors, in looking at these stories from a production standpoint, it takes us a week to shoot a half hour episode.
而我发现，从我们演员的角度来看，从制作的角度审视这些故事，我们拍一集半小时的剧要花一周时间。

489
00:20:46.990 --> 00:20:50.890
And then we go right into the next week of another episode.
然后紧接着下一周又要拍下一集。

490
00:20:51.810 --> 00:20:56.750
And when you look back on it, it's just kind of this wash of work, right?
当你回首往事时，那只是一段模糊的工作经历，对吧？

491
00:20:56.910 --> 00:21:04.550
And I don't, for me, it's very hard to kind of remember the specifics of episodes and the specifics of, like, what was in what episode.
对我来说，很难记住剧集的具体细节，也很难记住哪段情节是在哪一集里的。

492
00:21:05.150 --> 00:21:11.450
And, I mean, you guys have been really kind of studying them, so it's probably more front of mind for you.
我是说，你们一直在研究这些剧集，所以可能对你们来说印象更深。

493
00:21:11.450 --> 00:21:21.690
But I found this, going back and watching this episode, like, it did trigger a lot of memories.
但我发现，回头重看这一集，确实勾起了很多回忆。

494
00:21:21.690 --> 00:21:28.210
But it also was a little frustrating kind of realizing that what I don't remember.
但同时也感到有点沮丧，因为意识到自己记不清那么多东西了。

495
00:21:28.470 --> 00:21:29.250
And there are certain scenes.
而且有些场景。

496
00:21:29.250 --> 00:21:31.450
I don't know if you have this experience watching episodes of The Office.
我不知道你们在看《办公室》的时候有没有这种感觉。

497
00:21:31.490 --> 00:21:32.210
All the time.
经常有。

498
00:21:32.250 --> 00:21:34.150
Where you're like, I don't remember shooting that.
就是那种，我不记得拍过这一幕的感觉。

499
00:21:34.310 --> 00:21:34.890
I don't remember.
我不记得了。

500
00:21:34.890 --> 00:21:37.170
I don't even remember that day or what was going on.
我甚至不记得那天发生了什么，或者当时在干什么。

501
00:21:37.170 --> 00:21:41.390
And sometimes it's because you have some crazy thing going on in your life.
有时是因为你的生活中发生了一些疯狂的事情。

502
00:21:41.490 --> 00:21:45.390
But more often, I think it's just because you just don't remember every day at work.
但更多时候，我觉得只是因为你不记得工作中的每一天了。

503
00:21:46.350 --> 00:21:48.910
And I got a little heart sick kind of watching.
看着这些画面，我心里感到一阵难过。

504
00:21:49.090 --> 00:21:58.330
There were some parts of this episode where I was like, oh, boy, I wish I remembered, like, just, you know, that scene where we're all around the piano together.
这一集里有些片段让我觉得，天哪，我真希望自己还记得，比如我们大家围在钢琴旁的那一幕。

505
00:21:58.330 --> 00:22:03.390
And it's one of those rare scenes where almost everybody is, like, in a clump.
那是为数不多的几个几乎所有人都聚在一起的场景之一。

506
00:22:03.530 --> 00:22:05.750
And it's with positive energy, right?
而且充满了正能量，对吧？

507
00:22:05.870 --> 00:22:10.190
Usually it's like, you know, a meeting in the conference room.
通常情况就像是在会议室开会那样。

508
00:22:10.490 --> 00:22:10.540
Yeah.
是啊。

509
00:22:10.730 --> 00:22:11.130
It's all crazy.
那太疯狂了。

510
00:22:11.310 --> 00:22:15.890
But, like, to have a moment where everyone's kind of in a good place and happy.
但能有这样一个大家心情愉悦、相处融洽的时刻。

511
00:22:15.990 --> 00:22:20.670
It just, I remember watching that and thinking, like, this is so special.
我记得当时看的时候就在想，这真是太特别了。

512
00:22:20.670 --> 00:22:22.130
Like, I love these people.
我真的很爱这些人。

513
00:22:22.130 --> 00:22:23.310
I love these human beings.
我爱这些活生生的人。

514
00:22:24.150 --> 00:22:27.610
And it made me a little bit heart sick for the things I don't remember.
这让我对自己记不起来的事情感到有些难过。

515
00:22:28.210 --> 00:22:32.650
You're literally, your character has the line at the end where you say.
你饰演的角色在最后确实有句台词，你说。

516
00:22:32.870 --> 00:22:33.290
In the finale.
在结局里。

517
00:22:33.610 --> 00:22:37.150
You wish that you knew you were in the good times when you were in them.
你希望自己在身处美好时光时，能意识到那是美好时光。

518
00:22:37.470 --> 00:22:38.990
Like, that's literally what you're saying.
那真的是你的原话。

519
00:22:39.130 --> 00:22:39.890
It's so true, yeah.
确实如此，没错。

520
00:22:40.070 --> 00:22:40.770
But I get it.
但我明白。

521
00:22:40.790 --> 00:22:43.510
It is true, though, because you work every day.
不过这确实是真的，因为你每天都在工作。

522
00:22:43.730 --> 00:22:45.690
And some days stand out and some days don't.
有些日子令人难忘，而有些则不然。

523
00:22:45.850 --> 00:22:47.290
It doesn't matter what your job is.
无论你的工作是什么都一样。

524
00:22:47.550 --> 00:22:49.050
And acting is no different.
演戏也不例外。

525
00:22:49.050 --> 00:22:55.130
But sometimes I don't know the show the way people know it when they can just sit down
但有时我并不像观众那样了解这部剧，他们可以坐下来

526
00:22:55.130 --> 00:22:56.610
and watch it all the way through.
一口气看完。

527
00:22:56.950 --> 00:22:57.390
Right, right.
没错，没错。

528
00:22:57.530 --> 00:22:59.770
And we cross-borded episodes.
而且我们是交叉拍摄剧集的。

529
00:23:00.130 --> 00:23:00.370
Yeah, of course.
是啊，当然。

530
00:23:00.370 --> 00:23:04.770
Sometimes we shot three days in one episode and two days in another episode.
有时我们一天要拍三集的内容，第二天又拍另一集的内容。

531
00:23:04.870 --> 00:23:05.010
Right.
对。

532
00:23:05.010 --> 00:23:09.450
And it kind of becomes like when your kids mix all the Play-Doh together, you know,
这感觉就像你孩子把所有橡皮泥混在一起一样，你知道的，

533
00:23:09.570 --> 00:23:12.450
and you get that one big Play-Doh mound.
最后就变成了一大团橡皮泥。

534
00:23:12.610 --> 00:23:12.950
I don't know.
我不知道。

535
00:23:13.050 --> 00:23:13.970
That's not very articulate.
这个比喻不太贴切。

536
00:23:14.370 --> 00:23:15.710
I liked that metaphor.
我倒挺喜欢这个比喻的。

537
00:23:15.950 --> 00:23:16.370
I do, too.
我也喜欢。

538
00:23:16.370 --> 00:23:22.490
I feel like every conference room scene is one memory in my head.
我觉得脑海里所有的会议室场景都融合成了一个记忆。

539
00:23:22.610 --> 00:23:25.870
So many of these episodes I hadn't seen since we filmed them.
很多剧集我从拍摄完就没再看过。

540
00:23:26.090 --> 00:23:26.410
Crazy.
太疯狂了。

541
00:23:26.610 --> 00:23:29.910
But I'm so thankful for, like, a wonderful thing that we have.
但我非常感激我们拥有这样一段美妙的经历。

542
00:23:30.310 --> 00:23:30.830
Amen.
说得好。

543
00:23:31.210 --> 00:23:31.470
Yeah.
是啊。

544
00:23:31.670 --> 00:23:38.250
And when I do catch an episode here and there, it is like just hanging out with old friends.
当我偶尔看到一集时，感觉就像是在和老朋友叙旧。

545
00:23:38.510 --> 00:23:38.810
Yeah.
没错。

546
00:23:38.850 --> 00:23:39.710
It's just awesome.
那感觉真是太棒了。

547
00:23:39.710 --> 00:23:46.770
I don't think I ever lost the feeling of excitement walking onto set about what was
我想我从未失去过那种走进片场时对即将发生的事情的兴奋感。

548
00:23:46.770 --> 00:23:47.450
going to happen.
就是那种感觉。

549
00:23:47.630 --> 00:23:53.130
Like, what are these hilarious, wonderful people going to do to surprise me today?
比如，这些滑稽又可爱的人今天会给我带来什么惊喜？

550
00:23:54.270 --> 00:23:58.570
And like you were saying, conference room scenes, like, all of us getting in there, just being
就像你刚才说的，会议室的场景，我们所有人聚在那里，只是待着

551
00:23:58.570 --> 00:24:00.470
like this, something funny is going to happen.
就像这样，会有什么有趣的事情发生。

552
00:24:00.730 --> 00:24:01.990
Like, somebody is going to do something.
比如，有人要做点什么。

553
00:24:02.070 --> 00:24:02.850
We all have the script.
我们都有剧本。

554
00:24:02.990 --> 00:24:03.730
We know what we're going to say.
我们知道自己要说什么。

555
00:24:03.850 --> 00:24:06.970
But it's still like, I can't wait to see how BJ does this line.
但还是会觉得，我等不及想看BJ会怎么演这句台词。

556
00:24:07.030 --> 00:24:09.730
Or I can't wait to see how Oscar does this line.
或者我等不及想看奥斯卡会怎么演这句台词。

557
00:24:09.850 --> 00:24:13.010
And then, you know, take after take, it's just so warm and funny.
然后，你知道，一遍又一遍的拍摄，真的非常温馨有趣。

558
00:24:13.010 --> 00:24:18.490
And there are, of course, times that you get run down and you get tired and cranky.
当然，也有感到疲惫、劳累和暴躁的时候。

559
00:24:18.610 --> 00:24:27.310
But I always, always would walk into that soundstage, like, feeling excited and remembering back.
但我总是，总是会带着兴奋和回忆走进那个摄影棚。

560
00:24:27.390 --> 00:24:28.050
I mean, years.
我是说，好多年了。

561
00:24:28.210 --> 00:24:28.830
How many years?
多少年了？

562
00:24:29.030 --> 00:24:33.010
I worked on the show less than you guys, but seven years.
我参与节目的时间比你们短，但也有七年了。

563
00:24:33.230 --> 00:24:33.570
Almost as long.
差不多一样久。

564
00:24:33.670 --> 00:24:33.830
Yeah.
是啊。

565
00:24:34.010 --> 00:24:34.450
Seven years.
七年。

566
00:24:34.450 --> 00:24:40.750
And it just always walking on that stage was, was so like, just, just so fun.
每次走进那个舞台，真的，真的都特别开心。

567
00:24:40.950 --> 00:24:43.290
And like, what's going to happen?
而且，会发生什么呢？

568
00:24:43.830 --> 00:24:48.230
Well, Ed, before we let you go, can you tell us a little bit about your music?
好的，埃德，在你离开之前，能跟我们聊聊你的音乐吗？

569
00:24:48.750 --> 00:24:52.450
Are you performing anywhere with your banjo?
你最近有带着你的班卓琴去哪里演出吗？

570
00:24:52.750 --> 00:24:54.550
Are you still doing the bluegrass situation?
你还在做那个蓝草音乐项目吗？

571
00:24:55.430 --> 00:24:55.990
Yeah.
是的。

572
00:24:56.190 --> 00:25:01.270
So the bluegrasssituation.com is still very much alive and well.
所以bluegrasssituation.com依然活跃且运营良好。

573
00:25:01.270 --> 00:25:11.510
And that's a, that's just kind of a roots and folk, bluegrass music, kind of community, news, blog, hub.
那是一个关于根源音乐、民谣和蓝草音乐的社区、新闻、博客中心。

574
00:25:11.890 --> 00:25:13.010
And that's great.
那太棒了。

575
00:25:13.290 --> 00:25:17.670
I have pulled back from performing a lot in the last couple of years.
过去几年我减少了很多演出。

576
00:25:17.670 --> 00:25:28.070
I had kids and I'm just kind of focused elsewhere, but I still play all the time, especially for my kids, because they're a captive audience and they can't walk away.
我有了孩子，重心转移到了别处，但我还是经常弹，尤其是给孩子们弹，因为他们是我的忠实听众，而且他们没法走开。

577
00:25:28.070 --> 00:25:33.150
Um, and, and I'm eager to start getting back out there.
嗯，而且，我渴望重新开始去外面演出。

578
00:25:33.430 --> 00:25:33.830
Yeah.
是啊。

579
00:25:33.970 --> 00:25:40.270
I've been, I've been playing a lot and I'm starting to kind of get more serious about practicing and, and, and rehearsing,
我一直在练习，也开始更认真地对待练习和排练了，

580
00:25:40.350 --> 00:25:44.910
but there's not much going on in the professional space at this point.
但目前在专业领域还没有太多活动。

581
00:25:45.090 --> 00:25:46.350
Except Rutherford Falls.
除了《拉瑟福德瀑布》。

582
00:25:46.610 --> 00:25:46.890
Oh yeah.
哦，对。

583
00:25:46.910 --> 00:25:48.710
Season two is out now on Peacock.
第二季现在已经在Peacock上线了。

584
00:25:48.710 --> 00:25:49.430
Yes, indeed.
没错，确实。

585
00:25:49.650 --> 00:25:50.870
Rutherford Falls season two.
《拉瑟福德瀑布》第二季。

586
00:25:51.310 --> 00:26:01.170
Very, very proud of this show, uh, which I co-created with, um, uh, an, an amazing showrunner, Sierra Teller Ornelas and Michael Schur.
我为这部剧感到非常非常自豪，这是我和了不起的剧集主管塞拉·泰勒·奥内拉斯以及迈克尔·舒尔共同创作的。

587
00:26:01.450 --> 00:26:01.770
Yes.
是的。

588
00:26:02.190 --> 00:26:03.990
Who, uh, Office fans know well.
《办公室》的粉丝们对他很熟悉。

589
00:26:04.770 --> 00:26:05.730
That's going on.
正在热播中。

590
00:26:05.990 --> 00:26:06.750
We love it.
我们很喜欢。

591
00:26:06.990 --> 00:26:07.590
We love it.
我们很喜欢。

592
00:26:07.730 --> 00:26:09.210
Ed, I want to say two things to you.
埃德，我想对你说两件事。

593
00:26:09.990 --> 00:26:11.350
Banjo kids album.
班卓琴儿童专辑。

594
00:26:12.270 --> 00:26:12.790
Right?
对吧？

595
00:26:13.070 --> 00:26:15.450
That's a, that is a, that has crossed my mind.
那个，那个，我确实考虑过。

596
00:26:15.450 --> 00:26:19.790
I've been writing a lot of music lately and I think I'm going to, I, I, I just, I think.
我最近写了很多音乐，我想我可能会，我，我，我只是觉得。

597
00:26:20.030 --> 00:26:24.530
I would have loved that when Isabel was little because, you know, I, I don't know.
如果伊莎贝尔小时候有这个我会很喜欢，因为，你知道，我不知道。

598
00:26:24.690 --> 00:26:27.090
I had all the same songs that everyone had had forever.
我当时听的都是大家听了很久的那些老歌。

599
00:26:27.410 --> 00:26:32.590
And I, anytime there was a new kid's song that had any kind of a fun tune.
而且，每当有旋律有趣的儿童新歌出现时。

600
00:26:32.790 --> 00:26:33.390
Oh my gosh.
天哪。

601
00:26:33.490 --> 00:26:34.390
I got so excited.
我太激动了。

602
00:26:34.990 --> 00:26:35.430
All right.
好吧。

603
00:26:35.970 --> 00:26:36.270
All right.
好的。

604
00:26:36.290 --> 00:26:38.490
That might be the push I needed to get it done.
这可能就是我完成它所需要的动力。

605
00:26:38.830 --> 00:26:39.070
Okay.
好的。

606
00:26:40.370 --> 00:26:40.930
All right.
没问题。

607
00:26:41.050 --> 00:26:42.110
Ed, we love you so much.
埃德，我们太爱你了。

608
00:26:42.230 --> 00:26:44.630
Thank you so much for coming in the studio.
非常感谢你来到演播室。

609
00:26:44.630 --> 00:26:46.470
Yes, Ed is in here, you guys.
没错，埃德就在这儿，各位。

610
00:26:46.470 --> 00:26:46.930
I'm in the studio.
我在演播室里。

611
00:26:46.950 --> 00:26:48.030
He's sitting next to us.
他正坐在我们旁边。

612
00:26:48.150 --> 00:26:49.210
This is the table.
这就是那张桌子。

613
00:26:49.370 --> 00:26:50.590
Yes, we're here.
是的，我们在这儿。

614
00:26:51.090 --> 00:26:52.150
Thanks so much for having me.
非常感谢邀请我来。

615
00:26:52.330 --> 00:26:54.590
It's just so good to see you guys.
能见到你们真是太好了。

616
00:26:54.970 --> 00:26:55.590
It's wonderful.
这太棒了。

617
00:26:55.910 --> 00:26:56.530
Warm my heart.
暖心。

618
00:26:56.630 --> 00:26:57.030
I love you.
我爱你。

619
00:26:57.490 --> 00:26:58.710
Well, we're going to take a break.
好了，我们要休息一下。

620
00:26:58.710 --> 00:27:01.870
We're going to walk Ed out and then we'll be back to break down this episode.
我们要送埃德出去，然后回来继续解析这一集。

621
00:27:12.030 --> 00:27:14.790
Angela, I'm just going to be happy all day now because we got to hang out with Ed.
安吉拉，我今天一整天都会很开心，因为我们能和埃德待在一起。

622
00:27:14.970 --> 00:27:15.430
I know.
我知道。

623
00:27:15.890 --> 00:27:19.510
We should tell you guys, we've actually been chatting with him for like an hour.
我们得告诉大家，其实我们已经和他聊了一个小时了。

624
00:27:19.830 --> 00:27:22.030
We talked to Ed for two hours.
我们和埃德聊了两个小时。

625
00:27:22.270 --> 00:27:22.530
Yeah.
是啊。

626
00:27:22.850 --> 00:27:23.790
I didn't want him to leave.
我都不想让他走。

627
00:27:23.790 --> 00:27:24.370
Me either.
我也是。

628
00:27:24.650 --> 00:27:26.770
And we did finally have to let him go.
但我们最终还是不得不让他离开了。

629
00:27:27.070 --> 00:27:27.170
Yeah.
是啊。

630
00:27:27.430 --> 00:27:28.850
We have to finish this episode.
我们得把这一集录完。

631
00:27:29.050 --> 00:27:29.230
Yeah.
没错。

632
00:27:29.990 --> 00:27:35.950
Also during our break, we reached out to Randy and you guys, he's sending Cassie the audio
另外在休息期间，我们联系了兰迪，各位，他现在正把埃德唱的《我心永恒》的音频文件发给凯西。

633
00:27:35.950 --> 00:27:39.790
file of Ed singing, My Heart Will Go On, right now.
我们会在本集结尾播放它。

634
00:27:40.030 --> 00:27:41.890
We are going to play it at the end of the episode.
我们会在本集结尾播放它。

635
00:27:41.890 --> 00:27:42.650
I can't wait.
我等不及了。

636
00:27:42.910 --> 00:27:43.110
Yes.
是的。

637
00:27:43.330 --> 00:27:44.990
Definitely stick around to hear this.
一定要留下来听听这个。

638
00:27:45.190 --> 00:27:49.450
We heard it and it is truly, truly amazing.
我们听过了，真的，真的太棒了。

639
00:27:49.630 --> 00:27:50.650
Like I got chills.
我听得都起鸡皮疙瘩了。

640
00:27:50.910 --> 00:27:51.310
I know.
我知道。

641
00:27:51.310 --> 00:27:52.430
It was kind of a moment.
那真是一个特别的时刻。

642
00:27:52.590 --> 00:27:54.490
We're going to play the whole entire song.
我们要播放整首歌。

643
00:27:54.670 --> 00:27:55.950
Ed gave us his permission.
埃德已经授权给我们了。

644
00:27:56.910 --> 00:27:57.310
Enjoy.
敬请欣赏。

645
00:27:57.650 --> 00:27:58.450
But stick to the end.
但一定要听到最后。

646
00:27:58.510 --> 00:27:58.890
It's there.
它就在那儿。

647
00:27:59.010 --> 00:27:59.770
It'll be at the end.
它会在最后出现。

648
00:28:00.130 --> 00:28:00.530
Okay.
好的。

649
00:28:01.330 --> 00:28:03.050
Let's start breaking down this episode.
让我们开始解析这一集吧。

650
00:28:03.550 --> 00:28:04.950
We talked about this a little bit.
我们之前稍微聊过这个。

651
00:28:05.070 --> 00:28:07.850
This episode opens with this fantastic cold open.
这一集以一段精彩的开场戏拉开序幕。

652
00:28:08.010 --> 00:28:12.190
This performance of a musical number from Sweeney Todd surprises the whole bullpen.
这段来自《理发师陶德》的音乐剧表演让整个办公室的人都惊呆了。

653
00:28:12.190 --> 00:28:12.850
Yeah.
没错。

654
00:28:13.330 --> 00:28:16.630
And Michael is like, oh my gosh, I auditioned for this.
迈克尔当时就像是，天哪，我试镜过这个角色。

655
00:28:16.770 --> 00:28:18.470
When did the cast list go up?
演员表什么时候贴出来的？

656
00:28:18.550 --> 00:28:19.710
What part did I get?
我拿到了什么角色？

657
00:28:19.970 --> 00:28:21.510
How clueless is Michael?
迈克尔到底有多迟钝？

658
00:28:21.910 --> 00:28:24.190
We got a fan catch from Carrie F.
我们收到了一位来自日本的粉丝Carrie F.的来信，她说，

659
00:28:24.370 --> 00:28:29.190
in Japan who said, when Michael asks about the cast list,
当迈克尔询问演员表时，

660
00:28:29.370 --> 00:28:31.550
look at Creed's face in the background.
看看背景里克里德的表情。

661
00:28:31.550 --> 00:28:32.610
It is amazing.
太绝了。

662
00:28:32.610 --> 00:28:35.590
And I feel like everyone should pause to see it.
我觉得每个人都应该暂停画面看一看。

663
00:28:35.830 --> 00:28:36.630
Oh my goodness.
天哪。

664
00:28:36.790 --> 00:28:37.510
Did you look at it?
你看过了吗？

665
00:28:37.510 --> 00:28:38.150
I did.
我看过了。

666
00:28:38.390 --> 00:28:39.210
What's he doing?
他在做什么？

667
00:28:40.630 --> 00:28:43.550
It's hard to explain, but it is a great look.
很难形容，但那个表情真的很棒。

668
00:28:43.990 --> 00:28:49.330
He looks almost like he's responsible for not casting Michael.
他看起来就像是他负责决定不让迈克尔参演一样。

669
00:28:49.610 --> 00:28:51.190
Like, I don't want to...
就像是，我不想……

670
00:28:51.190 --> 00:28:53.190
It was his decision.
那是他的决定。

671
00:28:53.850 --> 00:28:54.890
It's amazing.
太神奇了。

672
00:28:55.190 --> 00:28:55.490
All right.
好吧。

673
00:28:55.530 --> 00:28:56.510
I have to go check that out.
我得去看看。

674
00:28:56.630 --> 00:28:57.150
Thanks, Carrie.
谢谢你，Carrie。

675
00:28:57.530 --> 00:28:59.850
I was so impressed with this opening musical number.
我对这段开场音乐剧印象非常深刻。

676
00:28:59.970 --> 00:29:01.570
I really thought we should hear these guys.
我真的觉得我们应该听听他们唱。

677
00:29:01.830 --> 00:29:02.630
Oh, let's do it.
哦，来吧。

678
00:29:03.890 --> 00:29:04.410
Annie?
安妮？

679
00:29:08.240 --> 00:29:10.280
Attend the tale of Sweeney Todd.
听听理发师陶德的故事。

680
00:29:11.780 --> 00:29:14.580
His skin was pale and his eye was odd.
他皮肤苍白，眼神怪异。

681
00:29:15.380 --> 00:29:16.180
Yes, let's do it.
没错，来吧。

682
00:29:16.180 --> 00:29:19.820
He gave the faces of gentle men who never thereafter were heard of again.
他面对的是那些从此销声匿迹的绅士们。

683
00:29:20.420 --> 00:29:23.060
He trod a path that few have trod.
他走过了一条鲜有人迹的路。

684
00:29:23.420 --> 00:29:24.660
It's Sweeney Todd.
他就是理发师陶德。

685
00:29:26.180 --> 00:29:28.360
The demon barber of Fleet Street.
弗利特街的恶魔理发师。

686
00:29:29.340 --> 00:29:30.440
Did you write this?
这是你写的吗？

687
00:29:30.920 --> 00:29:31.240
No.
不是。

688
00:29:31.600 --> 00:29:32.020
Who did?
那是谁写的？

689
00:29:32.120 --> 00:29:32.680
Stephen Sondheim.
斯蒂芬·桑德海姆。

690
00:29:32.900 --> 00:29:33.480
Who is he?
他是谁？

691
00:29:33.480 --> 00:29:36.920
Swing your razor wide.
挥动你的剃刀。

692
00:29:37.140 --> 00:29:40.320
Sweeney, hold it to the sky.
陶德，把它举向天空。

693
00:29:41.540 --> 00:29:56.610
A fan question from Miriam Ellen Utah who wanted to know,
来自犹他州的粉丝米里亚姆·艾伦问了一个问题，她想知道，

694
00:29:56.810 --> 00:29:59.870
how much did NBC pay in royalties for Sweeney Todd?
NBC为《理发师陶德》支付了多少版权费？

695
00:30:00.490 --> 00:30:06.990
Miriam said, typical grand rights can cost a small high school production thousands of dollars.
米里亚姆说，通常大型版权费可能让一所小型高中制作演出花费数千美元。

696
00:30:07.290 --> 00:30:08.570
What did you guys pay?
你们付了多少钱？

697
00:30:08.570 --> 00:30:13.370
Well, I checked with Randy Cordray, of course, and he said this really was a huge deal.
嗯，我当然咨询了兰迪·科德雷，他说这确实是一笔大买卖。

698
00:30:13.850 --> 00:30:19.190
Quote, we basically had to produce a full-blown community theater production of Sweeney Todd
引用他的话，我们基本上得制作一场完整的《理发师陶德》社区剧院演出，

699
00:30:19.190 --> 00:30:26.750
embedded into a full-blown episode of The Office, and negotiating the music rights was complicated.
并将其嵌入到《办公室》的一整集中，协商音乐版权非常复杂。

700
00:30:27.370 --> 00:30:34.430
He said, Eric Colgen, our post-producer, contacted the Universal Television Music Supervisor,
他说，我们的后期制作人埃里克·科尔根联系了环球电视音乐主管，

701
00:30:34.690 --> 00:30:37.470
Carrie Druton, about getting the sync rights.
嘉莉·德鲁顿，关于获取同步权的事。

702
00:30:38.110 --> 00:30:40.950
That meant that we were allowed to sing the song ourself.
这意味着我们获准自己演唱这首歌。

703
00:30:40.950 --> 00:30:43.910
We weren't going to, like, play a recorded soundtrack.
我们不会去播放录制好的背景音乐。

704
00:30:44.290 --> 00:30:46.010
Yeah, there's all these layers to it.
没错，这其中涉及很多层面。

705
00:30:46.170 --> 00:30:52.050
But we also had to get something called grand rights because we were going to air it on television.
但我们还必须获得所谓的“大版权”，因为我们要把它在电视上播出。

706
00:30:52.050 --> 00:30:52.890
Oh.
噢。

707
00:30:53.330 --> 00:30:58.810
There's a difference between just doing it on a stage and then committing it to television forever.
仅仅在舞台上表演和把它永久录制在电视上是有区别的。

708
00:31:00.230 --> 00:31:02.770
Stephen Sondheim had to sign off.
斯蒂芬·桑德海姆必须签字同意。

709
00:31:03.270 --> 00:31:04.910
They had to send him our script.
他们必须把我们的剧本寄给他。

710
00:31:05.750 --> 00:31:06.210
Really?
真的吗？

711
00:31:06.490 --> 00:31:06.810
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

712
00:31:07.150 --> 00:31:08.310
He read our script?
他读了我们的剧本？

713
00:31:08.370 --> 00:31:09.530
He read Andy's play.
他读了安迪的剧本。

714
00:31:09.850 --> 00:31:10.830
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

715
00:31:10.910 --> 00:31:11.450
Guess what?
你猜怎么着？

716
00:31:11.630 --> 00:31:11.890
What?
什么？

717
00:31:12.130 --> 00:31:12.950
He loved it.
他很喜欢。

718
00:31:13.090 --> 00:31:13.470
Aw!
哇！

719
00:31:13.770 --> 00:31:15.150
He gave us his blessing.
他给了我们他的祝福。

720
00:31:16.490 --> 00:31:23.730
Ultimately, we ended up paying $100,000, and we got the rights to sing four songs.
最终，我们支付了十万美元，获得了四首歌的演唱权。

721
00:31:24.230 --> 00:31:25.470
And that's how we did it.
我们就是这样完成的。

722
00:31:25.690 --> 00:31:25.970
Wow.
哇。

723
00:31:26.350 --> 00:31:28.650
I have a fan question from Sarah L.
我有一个来自得克萨斯州圣安东尼奥市萨拉·L的粉丝提问。

724
00:31:28.890 --> 00:31:30.210
in San Antonio, Texas.
你好啊，萨拉。

725
00:31:30.210 --> 00:31:30.990
What's up, Sarah?
你好，萨拉。

726
00:31:31.150 --> 00:31:31.730
Hi, Sarah.
你好，萨拉。

727
00:31:32.250 --> 00:31:34.390
Where did the singers come from for this episode?
这一集的歌手是从哪里找来的？

728
00:31:34.570 --> 00:31:36.050
Sarah, I love this question.
萨拉，我喜欢这个问题。

729
00:31:36.230 --> 00:31:37.210
We'll tell you all about it.
我们会告诉你一切。

730
00:31:37.370 --> 00:31:37.590
Yeah.
没错。

731
00:31:37.810 --> 00:31:40.890
All the singers were cast by our casting director, Allison Jones.
所有的歌手都是由我们的选角导演艾莉森·琼斯选定的。

732
00:31:40.890 --> 00:31:44.470
And our director for this episode was John Scott.
这一集的导演是约翰·斯科特。

733
00:31:44.910 --> 00:31:51.470
Before he directed The Office, he had directed episodes of Glee, and he'd also worked as a camera operator and cinematographer.
在执导《办公室》之前，他曾执导过《欢乐合唱团》的剧集，还担任过摄像师和摄影指导。

734
00:31:51.710 --> 00:31:59.290
So this kind of made him perfect because he knew how to blend musical performance and documentary-style shooting.
所以这让他成为了完美人选，因为他知道如何将音乐表演和纪录片式的拍摄手法融合在一起。

735
00:31:59.670 --> 00:32:03.950
This is the only episode of The Office that he directed, and thank goodness we got him for it.
这是他执导的唯一一集《办公室》，谢天谢地我们请到了他。

736
00:32:04.070 --> 00:32:04.510
I know.
我知道。

737
00:32:04.670 --> 00:32:05.690
He's a prolific director.
他是一位多产的导演。

738
00:32:05.690 --> 00:32:07.410
If you look him up, he's just done everything.
如果你去查一下，他几乎什么都做过。

739
00:32:07.410 --> 00:32:13.170
We also hired a musical supervisor for this episode, who Randy called a musical genius.
我们还为这一集聘请了一位音乐总监，兰迪称他为音乐天才。

740
00:32:13.550 --> 00:32:15.230
His name was Nathan Wang.
他的名字叫内森·王。

741
00:32:15.510 --> 00:32:23.590
He prepped all of the musical background tracks, attended all rehearsals, and he sat in on the auditions with Allison Jones and John Scott.
他准备了所有的音乐背景音轨，参加了所有的排练，并和艾莉森·琼斯以及约翰·斯科特一起参与了试镜。

742
00:32:23.790 --> 00:32:26.430
So the three of them found all of our singers.
所以他们三个人找齐了我们所有的歌手。

743
00:32:26.810 --> 00:32:27.110
Yes.
是的。

744
00:32:27.310 --> 00:32:32.930
And Nathan, if you listen to this, Randy could not say enough wonderful things about you.
内森，如果你在听的话，兰迪对你的赞美真是说都说不完。

745
00:32:33.070 --> 00:32:36.390
He just went on and on about how important you were for this episode.
他一直在夸你对这一集有多么重要。

746
00:32:36.390 --> 00:32:37.230
Yes.
是的。

747
00:32:37.490 --> 00:32:42.890
Randy also told us that this cold-open sequence was choreographed by Mary Ann Kellogg.
兰迪还告诉我们，这段开场戏是由玛丽·安·凯洛格编舞的。

748
00:32:43.010 --> 00:32:45.010
You guys remember she did the lip dub.
你们还记得她做过那个对口型表演吧。

749
00:32:45.250 --> 00:32:46.850
And here were the performers.
以下是表演者名单。

750
00:32:47.230 --> 00:32:49.270
Kelly Ebsery played the Beggar Lady.
凯莉·埃布瑟里饰演乞丐夫人。

751
00:32:49.530 --> 00:32:51.170
Maxwell Glick played Tobias.
马克斯韦尔·格利克饰演托拜厄斯。

752
00:32:51.630 --> 00:32:53.930
Heather Marie Marsden played Mrs. Lovett.
希瑟·玛丽·马斯登饰演洛维特夫人。

753
00:32:54.270 --> 00:32:56.590
David Kirk Grant played Castmate No.
大卫·柯克·格兰特饰演剧组成员编号

754
00:32:56.710 --> 00:32:56.990
2.
2。

755
00:32:57.670 --> 00:32:59.710
Erika Hanrahan Ball played Joanna.
埃里卡·汉拉汉·鲍尔饰演乔安娜。

756
00:33:00.470 --> 00:33:02.410
Harry Murphy played Judge Turpin.
哈里·墨菲饰演特平法官。

757
00:33:02.890 --> 00:33:04.690
Randy Gaia played Pirelli.
兰迪·盖亚饰演皮雷利。

758
00:33:04.690 --> 00:33:07.390
And Michael Tuba Heatherton played Beatle.
还有迈克尔·图巴·希瑟顿饰演披头士。

759
00:33:07.610 --> 00:33:08.830
What a fantastic group.
真是个了不起的团队。

760
00:33:09.110 --> 00:33:11.350
And lady, how fun was it to see Tuba?
还有，女士，看到图巴是不是很有趣？

761
00:33:11.590 --> 00:33:12.490
I know.
我知道。

762
00:33:12.710 --> 00:33:13.450
I know.
我知道。

763
00:33:13.570 --> 00:33:17.430
We should tell everybody who he is because he appeared on The Office several times.
我们应该告诉大家他是谁，因为他曾在《办公室》里出现过好几次。

764
00:33:17.590 --> 00:33:20.110
We even got a fan catch from Rob B.
我们甚至收到了来自加利福尼亚州洛杉矶的罗布·B发来的粉丝反馈，

765
00:33:20.190 --> 00:33:22.870
in Los Angeles, California, who said,
他说，

766
00:33:23.130 --> 00:33:25.430
Ladies, I think you need a Tuba Tracker.
女士们，我觉得你们需要一个“图巴追踪器”。

767
00:33:25.670 --> 00:33:26.950
Oh, a Tuba Tracker!
哦，图巴追踪器！

768
00:33:26.950 --> 00:33:32.890
This episode marks the first appearance of Michael Tuba Heatherton in the series.
这一集标志着迈克尔·图巴·希瑟顿在剧中的首次亮相。

769
00:33:33.370 --> 00:33:39.930
And he reprises this role in a deleted scene from Season 8, Episode 13, Jury Duty,
他还在第八季第十三集《陪审团义务》的删减片段中重演了这个角色，

770
00:33:40.150 --> 00:33:47.250
where he pretends to be a police officer, only to be recognized by Daryl as a member of Andy's play.
他在那里假装成一名警察，结果被达里尔认出是安迪剧团的成员。

771
00:33:47.250 --> 00:33:50.150
I look forward to that deleted scene, lady.
我很期待那个删减片段，女士。

772
00:33:50.390 --> 00:33:50.670
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

773
00:33:50.670 --> 00:33:57.330
But we will also see Tuba in The Seminar as an attendee of Andy's seminar.
但我们也会在《研讨会》那一集中看到图巴，他是安迪研讨会的参与者之一。

774
00:33:57.830 --> 00:34:05.910
And we're going to see two of Tuba's clown headshots in Roseanne's Talent Agency in Season 9.
我们还会在第九季的《罗珊的经纪公司》中看到两张图巴的小丑头像照。

775
00:34:05.910 --> 00:34:15.510
And finally, we're going to see him as the minister in Season 9, The Farm, and in the finale, marrying Dwight and Angela.
最后，我们会在第九季的《农场》以及大结局中看到他饰演牧师，为德怀特和安吉拉主持婚礼。

776
00:34:16.230 --> 00:34:18.370
He is just like Nelson Franklin.
他就像尼尔森·富兰克林一样。

777
00:34:18.690 --> 00:34:20.870
He is, because he played multiple roles.
确实，因为他饰演了多个角色。

778
00:34:20.910 --> 00:34:21.470
Multiple roles.
多个角色。

779
00:34:21.550 --> 00:34:22.590
Or maybe the same.
或者可能是一个人。

780
00:34:23.010 --> 00:34:26.130
Maybe he's a man who has many jobs.
也许他是一个身兼数职的人。

781
00:34:26.450 --> 00:34:26.810
Yeah.
是啊。

782
00:34:27.090 --> 00:34:29.230
Like the character Kirk on Gilmore Girls.
就像《吉尔莫女孩》里的柯克那个角色一样。

783
00:34:29.470 --> 00:34:30.550
He worked everywhere.
他到处打工。

784
00:34:30.810 --> 00:34:32.390
I have never seen Gilmore Girls.
我从来没看过《吉尔莫女孩》。

785
00:34:32.530 --> 00:34:33.450
Whoa, really?
哇，真的吗？

786
00:34:33.770 --> 00:34:34.050
Yeah.
真的。

787
00:34:34.410 --> 00:34:35.790
Oh, they talk real faSt.
哦，他们说话语速非常快。

788
00:34:35.910 --> 00:34:36.550
They do?
是吗？

789
00:34:36.690 --> 00:34:36.950
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

790
00:34:37.050 --> 00:34:37.990
Yeah, that was the thing.
是啊，那就是那部剧的特色。

791
00:34:38.130 --> 00:34:40.030
The dialogue, it comes out very, very faSt.
台词说出来非常、非常快。

792
00:34:40.770 --> 00:34:41.170
Oh.
哦。

793
00:34:41.890 --> 00:34:42.170
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

794
00:34:42.370 --> 00:34:43.590
Just a style choice?
这只是一种风格选择吗？

795
00:34:43.730 --> 00:34:43.990
Yes.
是的。

796
00:34:44.510 --> 00:34:45.090
I don't think I...
我觉得我可能……

797
00:34:45.090 --> 00:34:47.610
And you had to say your lines exactly as written.
而且你必须一字不差地按照剧本说台词。

798
00:34:48.370 --> 00:34:50.070
I would not do very well.
我肯定做不到。

799
00:34:50.910 --> 00:34:51.990
This is not the show.
那不是我的剧。

800
00:34:52.070 --> 00:34:53.430
It's good you were not cast on it.
幸好你没被选上。

801
00:34:53.470 --> 00:34:54.190
No, I was not.
不，我没有。

802
00:34:54.930 --> 00:34:55.850
Well, Rob B.
好吧，来自洛杉矶的

803
00:34:55.950 --> 00:34:57.570
from Los Angeles wants to know,
Rob B. 想问，

804
00:34:57.730 --> 00:35:03.310
is it just a happy coincidence that Tuba was cast in so many one-off roles on The Office?
Tuba 在《办公室》里出演了那么多一次性角色，这仅仅是巧合吗？

805
00:35:03.770 --> 00:35:05.190
Or is there another reason?
还是有别的原因？

806
00:35:05.570 --> 00:35:07.010
There is another reason.
确实有别的原因。

807
00:35:07.450 --> 00:35:09.190
First of all, Tuba's amazing.
首先，Tuba 非常棒。

808
00:35:09.430 --> 00:35:10.550
We love him.
我们很爱他。

809
00:35:10.770 --> 00:35:16.330
In addition to being extremely talented, Tuba was also married to our amazing script supervisor,
除了才华横溢之外，Tuba 当时还娶了我们出色的剧本主管，

810
00:35:16.690 --> 00:35:16.990
Theda.
Theda。

811
00:35:16.990 --> 00:35:17.570
Yeah.
没错。

812
00:35:18.310 --> 00:35:19.330
And Tuba was an actor.
而且 Tuba 是一名演员。

813
00:35:19.490 --> 00:35:20.810
He was a professional clown.
他是一位专业的小丑。

814
00:35:20.990 --> 00:35:22.950
Just an amazing person.
他真的是个很棒的人。

815
00:35:23.190 --> 00:35:29.570
Well, let's get into this episode because Andy has two comps for closing night of his show for Erin and her Gabe.
好了，我们进入这一集吧，因为安迪手里有两张他演出的闭幕之夜赠票，本来是给艾琳和她的盖博的。

816
00:35:29.570 --> 00:35:31.910
And he finds out Gabe isn't going.
结果他发现盖博不去了。

817
00:35:32.070 --> 00:35:33.470
He didn't think anyone else was going to go.
他以为没别人会去了。

818
00:35:34.290 --> 00:35:35.570
How happy is Andy?
安迪有多高兴？

819
00:35:35.930 --> 00:35:40.450
He is so happy until it looks like nobody else is coming.
他本来很高兴，直到发现好像没别人要来了。

820
00:35:41.210 --> 00:35:41.730
Like...
就像……

821
00:35:41.730 --> 00:35:42.070
Yeah.
是啊。

822
00:35:42.070 --> 00:35:44.330
Jim and Pam's babysitter fell through.
吉姆和帕姆的保姆临时来不了了。

823
00:35:44.730 --> 00:35:45.870
Michael's real sour.
迈克尔很不爽。

824
00:35:46.070 --> 00:35:46.890
He doesn't want to go.
他不想去。

825
00:35:47.110 --> 00:35:49.810
There was a series of talking heads here in the shooting draft,
在拍摄剧本里有一系列采访片段，

826
00:35:49.810 --> 00:35:52.610
and several people share their thoughts on musical theater.
好几个人分享了他们对音乐剧的看法。

827
00:35:53.210 --> 00:35:53.730
Oh.
哦。

828
00:35:53.970 --> 00:35:54.210
Yeah.
是啊。

829
00:35:54.210 --> 00:35:54.610
Yes.
没错。

830
00:35:54.810 --> 00:35:58.990
I really want to share with you what Stanley has to say and his feelings about standing ovations.
我真的很想和你们分享斯坦利是怎么说的，以及他对起立鼓掌的看法。

831
00:35:59.990 --> 00:36:04.090
I'll be there, but do not expect to stand an ovation.
我会去，但别指望我会起立鼓掌。

832
00:36:04.730 --> 00:36:09.810
I am sick of going to shows and feeling like I need to stand when the show isn't that good.
我厌倦了去看演出，明明演出没那么好，却感觉自己必须站起来。

833
00:36:10.270 --> 00:36:11.690
You hear me, Steve Harvey?
你听到了吗，史蒂夫·哈维？

834
00:36:15.270 --> 00:36:17.050
Throwing shade at Steve Harvey?
这是在内涵史蒂夫·哈维吗？

835
00:36:18.270 --> 00:36:19.890
I love this talking head.
我喜欢这段采访。

836
00:36:19.930 --> 00:36:20.670
I did, too.
我也喜欢。

837
00:36:21.330 --> 00:36:25.650
I've been to shows where everyone's standing up at the end.
我去看过演出，最后每个人都站了起来。

838
00:36:25.790 --> 00:36:28.170
It's almost like we stand up at the end of every show.
感觉就像我们每场演出结束时都会站起来一样。

839
00:36:28.330 --> 00:36:29.970
And then you feel bad if you don't.
如果你不站起来，还会觉得不好意思。

840
00:36:30.290 --> 00:36:30.570
Yeah.
是啊。

841
00:36:30.830 --> 00:36:31.910
And I had a little Stanley.
当时我心里也有点斯坦利附体了。

842
00:36:32.070 --> 00:36:35.570
I was like, well, how are they going to know when it's a real standing ovation?
我在想，那他们怎么知道什么时候才是真正的起立鼓掌呢？

843
00:36:36.450 --> 00:36:38.450
If we stand at the end of all of them?
如果每场演出结束我们都站起来的话？

844
00:36:38.570 --> 00:36:41.270
It's sort of like, you know, the participation prize.
这就像是那种参与奖一样。

845
00:36:41.670 --> 00:36:42.190
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

846
00:36:42.510 --> 00:36:46.010
But then I know what it takes to put on a theater production.
但后来我也知道筹备一场戏剧演出有多不容易。

847
00:36:46.290 --> 00:36:47.530
And you're like, you better stand.
所以你会觉得，你最好还是站起来吧。

848
00:36:47.570 --> 00:36:48.490
Just stand up.
就站起来吧。

849
00:36:48.530 --> 00:36:49.670
We worked our butts off.
我们可是拼了老命在做。

850
00:36:49.770 --> 00:36:50.090
Yeah.
没错。

851
00:36:50.670 --> 00:36:56.010
Just getting a show off the ground and from beginning to end, stand on up.
要把一档节目从无到有做起来，从头到尾，都得站稳脚跟。

852
00:36:56.390 --> 00:36:57.590
I feel both ways.
我感觉两种情绪都有。

853
00:36:58.030 --> 00:37:00.250
This talking head really made me laugh.
这个采访镜头真的把我逗乐了。

854
00:37:00.410 --> 00:37:05.410
And then also now when you rewatch this episode, at the end when they give a standing ovation,
而且现在重温这一集时，结尾大家起立鼓掌的时候，

855
00:37:05.410 --> 00:37:11.350
it cuts to Stanley and he's got the biggest grump face because he has to now stand and he's
镜头切到了斯坦利，他一脸极度不爽，因为他现在不得不站起来，

856
00:37:11.350 --> 00:37:12.030
really annoyed.
他真的很烦。

857
00:37:12.230 --> 00:37:12.710
You know what?
你知道吗？

858
00:37:12.710 --> 00:37:13.210
It's funny.
这很有趣。

859
00:37:13.390 --> 00:37:19.010
I know they cut the talking head, but everything about that shot of him like doing the obligatory
我知道他们剪掉了那个采访镜头，但那个镜头里他那种被迫

860
00:37:19.670 --> 00:37:21.850
standing ovation told me the whole story.
起立鼓掌的样子，已经说明了一切。

861
00:37:22.070 --> 00:37:22.170
Yep.
没错。

862
00:37:22.370 --> 00:37:24.070
I knew all his feelings about it.
我完全明白他的感受。

863
00:37:24.070 --> 00:37:29.210
Well, lady, Dwight is not going to go because the last time he went to the theater, a man
好吧，女士，德怀特是不会去的，因为上次他去看戏时，有个

864
00:37:29.210 --> 00:37:30.970
dressed as a cat sat on his lap.
打扮成猫的男人坐在了他的大腿上。

865
00:37:30.970 --> 00:37:33.870
I feel like Angela made him go to cats.
我觉得是安吉拉逼他去看《猫》的。

866
00:37:34.270 --> 00:37:36.790
Lady, we got so much mail from people.
女士，我们收到了好多观众来信。

867
00:37:36.990 --> 00:37:37.350
You did?
真的吗？

868
00:37:38.030 --> 00:37:39.010
Kobe S.
来自威斯康星州的

869
00:37:39.190 --> 00:37:40.690
from Wisconsin said,
科比·S说，

870
00:37:40.870 --> 00:37:45.670
in my mind, I have come to believe that Dwight attended a local production of cats to appease
在我看来，我一直认为德怀特是为了安抚安吉拉，才去看了当地制作的《猫》。

871
00:37:45.670 --> 00:37:46.130
Angela.
安吉拉。

872
00:37:46.370 --> 00:37:49.830
And I believe Andy was the cat who sat on Dwight's lap.
而且我相信安迪就是那个坐在德怀特腿上的猫。

873
00:37:51.370 --> 00:37:57.290
Because in season five, employee transfer, Andy dressed like a cat from a production of cats.
因为在第五季《员工调动》里，安迪就打扮成了《猫》剧里的猫。

874
00:37:57.550 --> 00:37:57.810
Yes.
没错。

875
00:37:58.410 --> 00:38:03.590
I was so curious about that line that I went to the shooting draft to see if it said something
我对那句台词太好奇了，于是去查了拍摄剧本，想看看上面有没有写

876
00:38:03.590 --> 00:38:07.830
like Dwight glances over at Angela, Angela rolls her eyes or something like that.
比如德怀特瞥了安吉拉一眼，安吉拉翻了个白眼之类的描述。

877
00:38:07.830 --> 00:38:11.290
It didn't, but I fully believe that Angela made him go to cats.
剧本里没写，但我完全相信是安吉拉逼他去看《猫》的。

878
00:38:11.590 --> 00:38:13.610
I'm with you and Kobe S.
我和你还有科比·S想的一样。

879
00:38:13.790 --> 00:38:14.510
Yes, Kobe.
没错，科比。

880
00:38:15.070 --> 00:38:16.590
Guess who wants to go to the play?
猜猜谁想去看戏？

881
00:38:17.030 --> 00:38:17.650
I know.
我知道。

882
00:38:18.030 --> 00:38:18.430
Angela.
安吉拉。

883
00:38:18.430 --> 00:38:22.310
Angela, I think this is proving the point that she goes to musicals.
安吉拉，我觉得这证明了她确实会去看音乐剧。

884
00:38:22.430 --> 00:38:24.990
And she says she would like Dwight to take her.
她说她想让德怀特带她去。

885
00:38:25.110 --> 00:38:27.370
And he's like, just disrobe.
而德怀特的意思是，直接脱衣服吧。

886
00:38:27.490 --> 00:38:28.750
Let's get to it, basically.
基本上就是说，咱们直接进入正题吧。

887
00:38:28.970 --> 00:38:29.690
And she's like, uh-uh.
而她的反应是，呃，不行。

888
00:38:29.970 --> 00:38:30.530
No, no, no.
不，不，不。

889
00:38:30.670 --> 00:38:32.950
You have to take me to the play to get the punch.
你得带我去看戏才能得到奖励。

890
00:38:33.570 --> 00:38:35.530
I have a location alert for this scene.
这一幕我有一个外景地提醒。

891
00:38:36.090 --> 00:38:37.370
Yes, it's a new location.
没错，这是一个新场景。

892
00:38:37.970 --> 00:38:39.710
This is Dwight's office.
这是德怀特的办公室。

893
00:38:40.130 --> 00:38:44.370
Now that he's the owner of the building, this is his business manager office.
既然他现在是这栋楼的业主，这就是他的物业经理办公室。

894
00:38:44.710 --> 00:38:47.790
Yes, and it's much nicer than his office at Dunder Mifflin.
没错，这比他在邓德·米夫林的办公室好多了。

895
00:38:47.950 --> 00:38:48.250
Yeah.
确实。

896
00:38:48.430 --> 00:38:49.110
That's true.
那是真的。

897
00:38:49.270 --> 00:38:49.950
He doesn't have.
他没有（独立办公室）。

898
00:38:50.070 --> 00:38:51.510
He's just part of a desk clump.
他只是办公桌群的一部分。

899
00:38:51.930 --> 00:38:57.630
Well, this was designed by Michael Gallenberg and built by Tim James, and it existed over on our warehouse set.
嗯，这是由迈克尔·加伦伯格设计，蒂姆·詹姆斯搭建的，它存在于我们的仓库布景里。

900
00:38:57.630 --> 00:39:05.870
At 4 minutes 28 seconds, did any of you guys notice the picture of the drone, the predator drone, big picture?
在4分28秒的时候，你们有人注意到那张无人机的照片了吗，那架捕食者无人机，很大的照片？

901
00:39:06.030 --> 00:39:06.470
It's tilted.
它是歪的。

902
00:39:06.690 --> 00:39:08.110
Yes, I did notice that.
是的，我注意到了。

903
00:39:08.110 --> 00:39:09.690
I was wondering why it was tilted.
我还在纳闷它为什么是歪的。

904
00:39:10.510 --> 00:39:12.210
I figured it had to be on purpose.
我以为这是故意的。

905
00:39:13.670 --> 00:39:16.810
I went to the shooting draft to see, and this is how it read.
我查了拍摄剧本，上面就是这么写的。

906
00:39:16.810 --> 00:39:19.210
Dwight is in his building management office.
德怀特在他的大楼管理办公室里。

907
00:39:19.210 --> 00:39:22.450
Dwight is in his building management office hanging a picture of a predator drone, and Angela enters.
德怀特正在他的大楼管理办公室里挂一张捕食者无人机的照片，安吉拉走了进来。

908
00:39:23.030 --> 00:39:24.850
Angela says, it's crooked.
安吉拉说，它挂歪了。

909
00:39:25.270 --> 00:39:29.210
Dwight says, yes, and if I come back and it's straight, I'll know someone was here.
德怀特说，没错，如果我回来发现它变直了，我就知道有人来过。

910
00:39:29.930 --> 00:39:31.690
Angela says, smart.
安吉拉说，聪明。

911
00:39:33.470 --> 00:39:38.850
And then she goes on to say, I want you to take me to the play this evening, and the scene continues as it aired.
然后她接着说，我要你今晚带我去看戏，场景就按照播出的那样继续下去了。

912
00:39:39.190 --> 00:39:42.610
Well, Dwight does agree to take her to the play, but he's not wearing a cape.
嗯，德怀特确实同意带她去看戏，但他没穿斗篷。

913
00:39:42.850 --> 00:39:43.210
Okay.
好吧。

914
00:39:44.250 --> 00:39:46.830
This made me realize, does he always wear a cape to plays?
这让我意识到，他去看戏总是穿斗篷吗？

915
00:39:47.070 --> 00:39:50.130
Like, he's not going to do his usual zhuzh for her.
就像是，他不会为了她做他平时那种精心打扮了。

916
00:39:50.370 --> 00:39:52.130
Yeah, has she asked in the past?
是啊，她以前要求过吗？

917
00:39:52.330 --> 00:39:53.450
And he wore a cape.
而且他还穿了斗篷。

918
00:39:53.590 --> 00:39:54.510
Maybe to cats.
也许是去看猫的时候穿的。

919
00:39:54.730 --> 00:39:55.030
Yes.
是的。

920
00:39:55.650 --> 00:40:01.610
Angela's going to have a talking head where she says, Dwight and I have a contractual agreement to procreate five times, plain and simple.
安吉拉会有一个单人访谈，她说，我和德怀特有一份生育五次子女的合同协议，简单明了。

921
00:40:01.930 --> 00:40:09.470
And should he develop feelings for me, well, that would be permissible under item 7C, clause 2, so I would not object.
如果他对我产生了感情，嗯，根据第7C条第2款，这是允许的，所以我不会反对。

922
00:40:10.130 --> 00:40:13.910
So, that little smile at the end that I do, I improvised.
所以，最后那个小微笑是我即兴发挥的。

923
00:40:14.310 --> 00:40:14.710
Oh.
哦。

924
00:40:14.830 --> 00:40:18.590
It wasn't in the shooting draft, and they really liked it, and they asked me to do it every time.
剧本里没写，但他们真的很喜欢，就要求我每次都这么做。

925
00:40:18.890 --> 00:40:21.130
Oh, I love when we would do things like that.
哦，我喜欢我们做那种事的时候。

926
00:40:21.290 --> 00:40:21.850
I know.
我知道。

927
00:40:21.850 --> 00:40:25.590
It was fun to see it again, because I remembered, all of a sudden, all those memories came back.
再次看到这一幕很有趣，因为我突然想起来了，所有的记忆都涌了回来。

928
00:40:25.610 --> 00:40:26.410
I was like, oh, yeah.
我当时心想，哦，没错。

929
00:40:26.670 --> 00:40:31.810
We thought maybe she would give away a little bit of her true feelings, just for a second.
我们想也许她会流露出一丁点真实情感，就一秒钟。

930
00:40:32.110 --> 00:40:34.610
It would always just fill me with such pride as an actor.
作为一名演员，这总是让我感到无比自豪。

931
00:40:34.610 --> 00:40:43.430
If I was there, performing for the director and the writer, and I did something with something they'd written for me, and they asked me to do it over and over again.
如果我在现场为导演和编剧表演，我对自己写的台词做了一些处理，而他们要求我一遍又一遍地重复那个动作。

932
00:40:43.430 --> 00:40:43.750
Yeah, yeah.
是啊，是啊。

933
00:40:43.930 --> 00:40:44.690
I was like, oh, yeah.
我当时心想，哦，没错。

934
00:40:44.770 --> 00:40:45.110
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

935
00:40:45.210 --> 00:40:45.650
I did it.
我做到了。

936
00:40:45.710 --> 00:40:46.070
I did it.
我做到了。

937
00:40:46.130 --> 00:40:46.410
I love it.
我喜欢这样。

