那是她的台词。

1567
01:08:12.460 --> 01:08:13.680
Over there in the office.
在那边的办公室里。

1568
01:08:13.740 --> 01:08:14.660
That's fantastic.
太棒了。

1569
01:08:15.500 --> 01:08:20.740
Dwight and Angela's scene will continue, and I wanted to read you guys the stage direction
Dwight和Angela的戏份还在继续，我想给你们读一下拍摄剧本里的

1570
01:08:20.740 --> 01:08:22.020
in the shooting draft.
舞台指导说明。

1571
01:08:22.420 --> 01:08:24.840
Oh, lady, I wrote it down, too.
噢，女士，我也把它记下来了。

1572
01:08:25.520 --> 01:08:31.940
Oh, it says, Angela stops and turns towards the wind, looking for her car.
噢，上面写着，Angela停下脚步，转向风吹来的方向，寻找她的车。

1573
01:08:32.180 --> 01:08:33.240
Looking as in quotes.
寻找，加了引号的。

1574
01:08:33.700 --> 01:08:35.920
The moon lights up her face.
月光照亮了她的脸。

1575
01:08:36.180 --> 01:08:38.000
The wind blows through her hair.
风吹过她的头发。

1576
01:08:38.000 --> 01:08:42.340
She looks stunning in a natural, normal way we've never seen.
她看起来美极了，是一种我们从未见过的、自然而又正常的美。

1577
01:08:42.700 --> 01:08:44.860
Dwight is taken aback.
Dwight大吃一惊。

1578
01:08:45.000 --> 01:08:47.240
I loved this phrasing.
我喜欢这种措辞。

1579
01:08:47.500 --> 01:08:51.460
A natural, normal way we've never seen.
一种我们从未见过的、自然而又正常的美。

1580
01:08:52.260 --> 01:08:56.000
And Lady Lexi T from Bermuda wrote in and said,
来自百慕大的Lexi T女士写信说，

1581
01:08:56.220 --> 01:08:58.660
Damn, Angela, you look amazing.
天哪，Angela，你看起来太惊艳了。

1582
01:08:58.660 --> 01:08:59.700
Go, lady.
加油，女士。

1583
01:08:59.960 --> 01:09:00.660
Thank you.
谢谢。

1584
01:09:00.660 --> 01:09:05.900
It was, it was, like, exactly perfect.
这真是，真是太完美了。

1585
01:09:06.440 --> 01:09:08.920
Did they have a fan to blow your hair?
他们有准备风扇来吹你的头发吗？

1586
01:09:09.160 --> 01:09:13.680
They had a fan, and I had to turn just right so my hair didn't blow across my face.
他们确实有风扇，我必须转到合适的角度，这样头发才不会吹到脸上。

1587
01:09:13.760 --> 01:09:14.060
Yeah.
是啊。

1588
01:09:14.060 --> 01:09:19.760
And they also put little twinkly lights in the trees to kind of make it look a little bit more,
而且他们还在树上挂了闪烁的小灯，为了让它看起来更，

1589
01:09:19.780 --> 01:09:20.740
you know, romantic.
你知道的，浪漫一点。

1590
01:09:21.000 --> 01:09:21.320
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1591
01:09:21.620 --> 01:09:27.880
This scene was really fun to do, especially playing someone who was so buttoned up for years
这场戏拍起来真的很有趣，尤其是扮演一个多年来一直如此保守的人，

1592
01:09:27.880 --> 01:09:31.500
to finally just even be in a normal outfit.
终于能穿上一套正常的衣服了。

1593
01:09:31.960 --> 01:09:32.360
Yeah.
是啊。

1594
01:09:33.100 --> 01:09:35.800
Here's how the scene continued in the shooting draft.
以下是拍摄剧本中这场戏的后续内容。

1595
01:09:36.180 --> 01:09:38.080
Angela leans in to Dwight.
Angela向Dwight靠过去。

1596
01:09:38.240 --> 01:09:40.100
She reaches for his pants.
她伸手去摸他的裤子。

1597
01:09:40.560 --> 01:09:41.480
Dwight sighs.
Dwight叹了口气。

1598
01:09:41.480 --> 01:09:45.100
She reaches into his pocket and pulls out the hole punch.
她伸手进他的口袋，掏出了打孔机。

1599
01:09:45.580 --> 01:09:47.260
Dwight says, Was that in the way?
Dwight说，那东西碍事吗？

1600
01:09:47.360 --> 01:09:48.000
Get rid of it.
把它扔掉。

1601
01:09:48.160 --> 01:09:50.520
She punches the card and hands it back to him.
她打完卡，把卡递还给他。

1602
01:09:50.860 --> 01:09:51.840
Good night, Dwight.
晚安，德怀特。

1603
01:09:52.580 --> 01:09:53.960
Angela climbs in her car.
安吉拉坐进她的车里。

1604
01:09:54.460 --> 01:09:57.040
Dwight watches her, completely frustrated.
德怀特看着她，一脸挫败。

1605
01:09:57.820 --> 01:09:58.260
Yeah.
是啊。

1606
01:09:58.900 --> 01:10:00.900
He wanted to get it on, and she was like,
他想亲热一下，而她却说，

1607
01:10:00.960 --> 01:10:01.320
No, no.
不行，不行。

1608
01:10:01.540 --> 01:10:02.300
This will count.
这算数。

1609
01:10:02.460 --> 01:10:03.860
Just coming to the play with me.
就当是陪我来看戏了。

1610
01:10:04.460 --> 01:10:05.800
She's leaving him wanting more.
她让他意犹未尽。

1611
01:10:06.000 --> 01:10:06.360
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1612
01:10:06.720 --> 01:10:10.320
We had to figure out exactly how we were going to choreograph that scene.
我们得弄清楚到底该怎么编排那场戏。

1613
01:10:10.320 --> 01:10:12.520
And, you know, Rain is so much taller than me.
而且，你知道，雷恩比我高得多。

1614
01:10:12.660 --> 01:10:12.920
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1615
01:10:12.920 --> 01:10:15.980
So we were trying to figure out what their embrace looked like.
所以我们在琢磨他们拥抱时是什么样子。

1616
01:10:16.140 --> 01:10:18.240
And, you know, he picked me up fairly easily.
你知道，他抱起我来还挺轻松的。

1617
01:10:18.240 --> 01:10:19.340
So we went with that.
所以我们就决定这么演了。

1618
01:10:20.160 --> 01:10:22.320
We had a fan catch from Maddie M.
我们收到了一位来自明尼阿波利斯的粉丝麦迪·M的来信，

1619
01:10:22.400 --> 01:10:23.920
in Minneapolis who said,
她说，

1620
01:10:24.160 --> 01:10:24.840
Old tech alert.
老式科技警报。

1621
01:10:25.060 --> 01:10:30.240
At 17 minutes and 20 seconds, Angela had to use the key to manually unlock her car door.
在17分20秒时，安吉拉不得不使用钥匙手动解锁车门。

1622
01:10:30.500 --> 01:10:30.960
Yes!
没错！

1623
01:10:31.760 --> 01:10:35.540
Backstage at the after party, Michael can be found eating dried apricots.
在后台的庆功派对上，迈克尔在吃杏干。

1624
01:10:35.740 --> 01:10:37.560
He's eaten 30 of them.
他吃了30个。

1625
01:10:37.900 --> 01:10:39.440
I had to look that up, lady.
我得查查这个，女士。

1626
01:10:39.600 --> 01:10:40.580
That seemed like too many.
这听起来太多了。

1627
01:10:41.480 --> 01:10:44.760
He's had 30 dried apricots and a bunch of red wine.
他吃了30个杏干，还喝了一堆红酒。

1628
01:10:45.260 --> 01:10:47.220
How's the rest of that evening going to play out?
那天晚上剩下的时间会怎么过呢？

1629
01:10:47.380 --> 01:10:52.500
Well, I'll tell you, the recommended daily consumption of dried apricots is 3 to 4 per day.
嗯，我告诉你，杏干的建议每日摄入量是每天3到4个。

1630
01:10:52.560 --> 01:10:52.920
What?
什么？

1631
01:10:53.040 --> 01:10:53.960
He ate 30?
他吃了30个？

1632
01:10:53.960 --> 01:10:56.460
He's eaten 10 times, the recommended amount.
他吃了建议量的10倍。

1633
01:10:56.560 --> 01:10:57.080
Oh, no.
噢，不。

1634
01:10:57.300 --> 01:11:00.560
It was about 480 calories of dried apricots.
那大约有480卡路里的杏干。

1635
01:11:00.720 --> 01:11:09.160
And if you eat too much dried fruit in one sitting, it can cause gas, abdominal cramping, bloating, constipation, or possibly diarrhea.
如果你一次吃太多干果，会导致胀气、腹部绞痛、腹胀、便秘，或者可能腹泻。

1636
01:11:09.480 --> 01:11:09.780
Oh.
噢。

1637
01:11:10.040 --> 01:11:11.100
So that's what...
所以这就是……

1638
01:11:11.100 --> 01:11:12.280
That's what's ahead of Michael.
这就是迈克尔接下来要面对的。

1639
01:11:12.440 --> 01:11:13.460
He has coming.
他要倒霉了。

1640
01:11:14.080 --> 01:11:19.760
This is when Sweeney Todd, who was played by Robert Mamana, comes up.
这时，由罗伯特·马马纳饰演的斯威尼·托德走了过来。

1641
01:11:20.040 --> 01:11:21.720
Daryl says, You crushed it.
达里尔说，你演得太棒了。

1642
01:11:21.760 --> 01:11:22.340
You did great.
你做得很好。

1643
01:11:22.340 --> 01:11:25.460
And he sees Michael and says, You're the guy that booed me.
然后他看到了迈克尔，说，你就是那个嘘我的人。

1644
01:11:26.740 --> 01:11:28.700
Michael's like, There are a lot of people booing you.
迈克尔说，嘘你的人多了去了。

1645
01:11:28.860 --> 01:11:30.040
It wasn't just me.
又不只是我一个。

1646
01:11:31.180 --> 01:11:33.000
And he's like, No, it was you.
他说，不，就是你。

1647
01:11:33.400 --> 01:11:35.560
And Daryl really calls Michael out on it.
达里尔真的当面指出了迈克尔的行为。

1648
01:11:35.600 --> 01:11:36.760
He's like, How would you like that?
他说，你觉得这样感觉如何？

1649
01:11:36.900 --> 01:11:38.220
And he starts booing him.
然后他开始嘘迈克尔。

1650
01:11:38.620 --> 01:11:40.280
Michael doesn't like it at all.
迈克尔一点也不喜欢这样。

1651
01:11:40.960 --> 01:11:44.280
The actor who played Sweeney Todd has done a ton of stuff.
饰演斯威尼·托德的那位演员演过很多作品。

1652
01:11:44.460 --> 01:11:47.580
He's done television dramas, but also a ton of theater.
他演过电视剧，也演过大量的戏剧。

1653
01:11:47.980 --> 01:11:51.520
He graduated from the University of Arizona with a Bachelor of Fine Arts,
他毕业于亚利桑那大学，获得了艺术学士学位，

1654
01:11:51.520 --> 01:11:54.980
and he has been nominated and won several awards for theater.
并且曾多次获得戏剧奖项提名并获奖。

1655
01:11:55.240 --> 01:11:56.380
He really was our ringer.
他真的是我们的王牌。

1656
01:11:56.800 --> 01:11:57.020
Yeah.
没错。

1657
01:11:57.300 --> 01:12:02.480
Well, Andy and Erin are going to have just, you know, their usual sweet but weird scene.
安迪和艾琳会有一场，你知道的，他们那种一贯甜蜜又古怪的戏份。

1658
01:12:02.700 --> 01:12:02.920
Yep.
是啊。

1659
01:12:03.080 --> 01:12:06.940
Where Andy is going to show her how Sweeney Todd would kill people in the barber chair.
安迪会向她展示斯威尼·托德是如何在理发椅上杀人的。

1660
01:12:06.940 --> 01:12:09.860
And they're just having the best time.
他们玩得非常开心。

1661
01:12:10.040 --> 01:12:13.420
And she says, I'm so glad we're hanging out outside of work again.
然后她说，真高兴我们又能下班后一起聚聚了。

1662
01:12:13.920 --> 01:12:14.140
Yeah.
是啊。

1663
01:12:14.420 --> 01:12:18.180
And then he takes her into the audience, and he shows her where her seats would have been,
接着他带她走进观众席，告诉她原本她的座位应该在哪里，

1664
01:12:18.420 --> 01:12:21.220
how it's the exact perfect spot.
那是多么完美的位置。

1665
01:12:21.220 --> 01:12:23.100
To get the right acoustics.
为了获得最佳的音响效果。

1666
01:12:23.200 --> 01:12:25.900
It seems far back, but it's actually the best sound.
看起来离得挺远，但其实那里的声音效果最好。

1667
01:12:26.420 --> 01:12:28.160
And that's when Gabe calls.
就在这时盖博打来了电话。

1668
01:12:28.360 --> 01:12:29.560
He needs some soup.
他想喝点汤。

1669
01:12:30.280 --> 01:12:30.720
Gabe.
盖博。

1670
01:12:30.940 --> 01:12:32.840
They've really written him like a wet blanket.
他们把他写得真像个扫兴鬼。

1671
01:12:33.000 --> 01:12:33.620
He is.
确实是。

1672
01:12:33.760 --> 01:12:34.580
It's true.
没错。

1673
01:12:35.660 --> 01:12:39.060
Well, Jim and Pam get home, and they have that classic parent moment
吉姆和帕姆回到家，他们遇到了那种经典的父母时刻，

1674
01:12:39.060 --> 01:12:41.080
where the kid is happy in the car seat.
孩子在安全座椅里睡得很香。

1675
01:12:41.160 --> 01:12:42.200
Maybe she's fallen asleep.
也许她已经睡着了。

1676
01:12:42.560 --> 01:12:46.200
And they know if they get her out of that car seat, she's going to wake up.
他们知道如果把她从安全座椅里抱出来，她就会醒。

1677
01:12:46.200 --> 01:12:50.480
So they decide to have their own nightcap out in the car.
所以他们决定在车里喝杯睡前酒。

1678
01:12:50.800 --> 01:12:54.120
Well, we got a fan question, Ange, from Samantha G.
安吉，我们收到一个粉丝提问，来自佛罗里达州的萨曼莎·G，

1679
01:12:54.160 --> 01:12:55.840
in Florida, who said,
她说，

1680
01:12:56.380 --> 01:12:59.080
This is more of a request than a question.
与其说是提问，不如说是个请求。

1681
01:12:59.740 --> 01:13:02.900
In a continuation of your scotch and Splendous sampling.
为了延续你们之前品尝苏格兰威士忌加代糖的活动。

1682
01:13:03.220 --> 01:13:03.270
Oh, no.
噢，不。

1683
01:13:03.270 --> 01:13:05.840
No, we're not going to have Irish cream and orange juice.
不，我们才不要喝爱尔兰奶油加橙汁。

1684
01:13:05.940 --> 01:13:06.240
No.
不行。

1685
01:13:06.520 --> 01:13:11.580
Samantha said, I wanted to see if you would be willing to brave orange juice and Irish cream.
萨曼莎说，我想看看你们愿不愿意挑战一下橙汁加爱尔兰奶油。

1686
01:13:11.920 --> 01:13:12.440
Samantha.
萨曼莎。

1687
01:13:14.000 --> 01:13:16.340
It sounds like a terrible combination,
听起来是个糟糕的组合，

1688
01:13:16.340 --> 01:13:20.280
but I'd love for you ladies to take one for the team and give it a try.
但我很希望你们两位女士能为团队做出牺牲，试一试。

1689
01:13:21.080 --> 01:13:24.060
So, lady, I brought in some Irish cream and orange juice.
所以，女士们，我带来了爱尔兰奶油和橙汁。

1690
01:13:24.140 --> 01:13:24.320
You did not.
你没带吧。

1691
01:13:24.420 --> 01:13:27.660
I cannot believe you brought Irish cream and orange juice.
真不敢相信你竟然带了爱尔兰奶油和橙汁。

1692
01:13:27.720 --> 01:13:28.280
I'll go get it.
我去拿。

1693
01:13:28.380 --> 01:13:29.040
It's in the fridge.
在冰箱里。

1694
01:13:29.160 --> 01:13:31.100
Are you supposed to refrigerate Irish cream?
爱尔兰奶油需要冷藏吗？

1695
01:13:31.320 --> 01:13:31.960
I don't know.
我不知道。

1696
01:13:32.040 --> 01:13:32.360
I've never even had it.
我甚至从来没喝过。

1697
01:13:32.360 --> 01:13:33.240
I wasn't sure.
我不确定。

1698
01:13:33.460 --> 01:13:34.740
I've never had Irish cream.
我从来没喝过爱尔兰奶油。

1699
01:13:34.760 --> 01:13:37.120
It's like whiskey and cream, right?
那是威士忌加奶油，对吧？

1700
01:13:37.380 --> 01:13:39.600
And you mix that with orange juice?
然后你要把它和橙汁混在一起？

1701
01:13:39.820 --> 01:13:42.180
I mean, normally you put it in your coffee, I think.
我的意思是，通常你应该把它加进咖啡里，我想。

1702
01:13:42.180 --> 01:13:42.780
Oh, yoy.
噢，天哪。

1703
01:13:43.300 --> 01:13:44.340
It's, yeah.
是啊，没错。

1704
01:13:44.620 --> 01:13:44.980
All right.
好吧。

1705
01:13:45.040 --> 01:13:45.520
I'll go get it.
我去拿。

1706
01:13:45.920 --> 01:13:46.340
All right.
好的。

1707
01:13:46.480 --> 01:13:50.380
Jenna has gotten the Irish cream and orange juice.
珍娜拿来了爱尔兰奶油和橙汁。

1708
01:13:50.660 --> 01:13:50.900
I have it.
我拿到了。

1709
01:13:50.960 --> 01:13:54.340
Now, I don't know what proportions I'm doing here.
现在，我不知道该按什么比例调配。

1710
01:13:55.120 --> 01:13:58.440
I'm so sad that Sam isn't here today.
山姆今天没来，我真难过。

1711
01:13:58.440 --> 01:14:01.560
I feel like he would want to be a part of this.
我觉得他肯定想参与进来。

1712
01:14:01.700 --> 01:14:04.140
Sorry, Sam, but you're on a lovely vacation.
抱歉了山姆，但你在享受美好的假期。

1713
01:14:04.800 --> 01:14:06.820
Abby, our guest engineer, surprise.
艾比，我们的客座工程师，惊喜吧。

1714
01:14:07.260 --> 01:14:09.480
You get Irish cream and orange juice.
给你爱尔兰奶油和橙汁。

1715
01:14:09.900 --> 01:14:11.280
Just what you've always wanted.
正是你一直想要的。

1716
01:14:11.280 --> 01:14:13.800
This probably disgusting drink.
这杯大概很恶心的饮料。

1717
01:14:14.940 --> 01:14:16.400
What do I, what do you think?
我该怎么做，你觉得呢？

1718
01:14:16.400 --> 01:14:18.640
How much orange juice and how much Irish cream?
橙汁和爱尔兰奶油各放多少？

1719
01:14:19.380 --> 01:14:21.980
I feel like it should be mostly orange juice, right?
我觉得应该以橙汁为主，对吧？

1720
01:14:21.980 --> 01:14:23.120
I mean, no, not on me.
我是说，不，别问我。

1721
01:14:23.300 --> 01:14:24.440
Go light on orange juice.
橙汁少放点。

1722
01:14:24.820 --> 01:14:26.060
Light on orange juice?
橙汁少放点？

1723
01:14:26.200 --> 01:14:27.300
Heavy on Irish cream?
爱尔兰奶油多放点？

1724
01:14:27.460 --> 01:14:27.800
Well.
嗯。

1725
01:14:27.960 --> 01:14:29.680
Am I supposed to shake this first?
我是不是应该先摇匀？

1726
01:14:29.860 --> 01:14:31.340
Why do I feel like I should shake it?
为什么我觉得我应该摇一下？

1727
01:14:31.860 --> 01:14:33.220
No, don't shake it.
不，别摇。

1728
01:14:33.460 --> 01:14:34.280
Don't shake it?
别摇？

1729
01:14:34.380 --> 01:14:35.220
Found a recipe.
找到了个配方。

1730
01:14:35.820 --> 01:14:37.880
Oh, there's a recipe?
噢，还有配方？

1731
01:14:38.220 --> 01:14:38.620
Yeah.
是啊。

1732
01:14:38.760 --> 01:14:43.720
It looks like five-eighths a cup of Irish cream and then one and a half cups orange juice.
看起来是五分之八杯的爱尔兰奶油，然后是一杯半的橙汁。

1733
01:14:44.180 --> 01:14:46.180
So it's mostly orange juice.
所以主要是橙汁。

1734
01:14:46.300 --> 01:14:46.560
Yeah.
没错。

1735
01:14:47.320 --> 01:14:47.780
All right.
好吧。

1736
01:14:48.060 --> 01:14:48.320
Okay.
行。

1737
01:14:49.000 --> 01:14:52.200
And then you are supposed to stir it or try blending it.
然后你应该搅拌它或者试着混合一下。

1738
01:14:52.600 --> 01:14:53.520
Blending it?
混合？

1739
01:14:54.280 --> 01:14:55.400
Well, you know what?
好吧，你知道吗？

1740
01:14:55.520 --> 01:14:57.240
Jim and Pam didn't blend anything.
吉姆和帕姆什么都没混合。

1741
01:14:57.620 --> 01:14:57.760
So.
所以。

1742
01:14:57.900 --> 01:14:58.120
I'm.
我。

1743
01:14:58.280 --> 01:14:59.780
Oh, it's curdling.
噢，它结块了。

1744
01:15:00.080 --> 01:15:00.560
That looks disgusting.
看起来真恶心。

1745
01:15:01.080 --> 01:15:02.540
We need to stir it.
我们需要搅拌一下。

1746
01:15:02.840 --> 01:15:03.840
It's not.
它没。

1747
01:15:03.840 --> 01:15:05.720
It's not mixing it together.
它没能混合在一起。

1748
01:15:06.100 --> 01:15:09.320
It looks like someone vomited in their orange juice.
看起来就像有人把呕吐物吐进了橙汁里。

1749
01:15:10.200 --> 01:15:11.480
Angela, this is yours.
安吉拉，这是你的。

1750
01:15:11.480 --> 01:15:13.200
It's more Irish cream.
这是更多的爱尔兰奶油。

1751
01:15:13.400 --> 01:15:13.450
Oh, no.
噢，不。

1752
01:15:13.560 --> 01:15:13.920
Follow the recipe.
照着食谱做。

1753
01:15:13.920 --> 01:15:14.820
That's what you said.
你之前也是这么说的。

1754
01:15:15.020 --> 01:15:19.100
You wanted it with the more weird curdling stuff.
是你自己想要加那种更奇怪的凝乳物质的。

1755
01:15:19.320 --> 01:15:20.900
We need something to stir it.
我们需要什么东西来搅拌一下。

1756
01:15:21.000 --> 01:15:21.960
I'm going to go get a spoon.
我去拿把勺子。

1757
01:15:22.120 --> 01:15:22.420
Okay.
好的。

1758
01:15:22.740 --> 01:15:23.480
Hold, please.
请稍等。

1759
01:15:24.360 --> 01:15:24.880
Okay.
好的。

1760
01:15:25.920 --> 01:15:26.860
Here's a spoon.
勺子来了。

1761
01:15:30.430 --> 01:15:32.310
It's not really helping that much.
这好像没什么大用。

1762
01:15:32.310 --> 01:15:34.730
The spoon is not doing anything.
这勺子根本起不到作用。

1763
01:15:35.090 --> 01:15:36.970
These two liquids don't want to go together.
这两种液体就是不想融合在一起。

1764
01:15:37.170 --> 01:15:38.030
That's clear to me.
这一点我很清楚。

1765
01:15:41.250 --> 01:15:41.770
Okay.
好吧。

1766
01:15:41.770 --> 01:15:42.230
Here we go.
开始了。

1767
01:15:42.490 --> 01:15:45.010
Cassie, Abby, they are not running in.
凯西，艾比，她们没跑过来。

1768
01:15:45.170 --> 01:15:49.150
Other times, I mean, there's no movement from them.
以前的话，我是说，她们一点动静都没有。

1769
01:15:49.150 --> 01:15:50.610
They have not left their chairs.
她们连椅子都没离开过。

1770
01:15:50.850 --> 01:15:52.210
They clearly don't want to drink.
她们显然不想喝。

1771
01:15:52.290 --> 01:15:53.130
You don't have to.
你没必要非得喝。

1772
01:15:53.350 --> 01:15:58.110
I want to go on record that for my beet vodka, people came in here at least at a quicker pace
我要郑重声明，当初我做甜菜伏特加的时候，大家跑进来的速度至少比现在快多了。

1773
01:15:58.110 --> 01:15:58.470
than this.
比这快。

1774
01:15:58.470 --> 01:15:58.610
Oh, yeah.
噢，确实。

1775
01:15:58.610 --> 01:16:00.110
I was excited for beet vodka.
我当时对甜菜伏特加可是很期待的。

1776
01:16:00.310 --> 01:16:02.470
This looks really scary.
这看起来真的很吓人。

1777
01:16:02.650 --> 01:16:02.830
Yeah.
确实。

1778
01:16:02.910 --> 01:16:03.810
It looks disgusting.
看起来真恶心。

1779
01:16:04.370 --> 01:16:08.010
Abby did not know what she was getting into when she was like, I'd love to fill in for
艾比当初说“我很乐意替萨姆代班”的时候，根本不知道自己要面对什么。

1780
01:16:08.010 --> 01:16:08.730
Sam today.
萨姆今天。

1781
01:16:08.850 --> 01:16:09.830
Everyone say hi, Abby.
大家跟艾比打个招呼吧。

1782
01:16:10.050 --> 01:16:10.550
Here we go.
开始了。

1783
01:16:10.610 --> 01:16:11.030
Here we go.
开始了。

1784
01:16:12.710 --> 01:16:13.710
Oh, it's not bad.
噢，味道还行。

1785
01:16:14.130 --> 01:16:14.530
Yeah.
是啊。

1786
01:16:14.630 --> 01:16:16.350
It kind of tastes like a creamsicle.
喝起来有点像奶油冰棒。

1787
01:16:16.510 --> 01:16:17.170
Creamsicle, yeah.
奶油冰棒，没错。

1788
01:16:17.390 --> 01:16:17.950
It is.
确实是。

1789
01:16:18.030 --> 01:16:19.070
It tastes like a creamsicle.
尝起来就像奶油冰棒。

1790
01:16:19.150 --> 01:16:19.610
Yeah.
是啊。

1791
01:16:19.990 --> 01:16:21.750
It's not as bad as it looks.
没看起来那么糟糕。

1792
01:16:21.950 --> 01:16:23.450
It looks really gross.
看起来真的很恶心。

1793
01:16:23.590 --> 01:16:24.410
It looks disgusting.
看起来真让人反胃。

1794
01:16:24.670 --> 01:16:26.310
I can't taste any of the alcohol.
我一点酒精味都喝不出来。

1795
01:16:26.390 --> 01:16:28.770
It just sort of tastes like creamy orange juice.
喝起来就像奶油橙汁。

1796
01:16:29.170 --> 01:16:30.710
It's not the worst thing in the world.
还不算世界上最难喝的东西。

1797
01:16:31.130 --> 01:16:33.790
Well, paint me surprised.
好吧，真是让我大吃一惊。

1798
01:16:34.790 --> 01:16:35.270
Yeah.
是啊。

1799
01:16:35.530 --> 01:16:37.570
I mean, scotch and Splenda, total surprise.
我是说，苏格兰威士忌加代糖，真是个大惊喜。

1800
01:16:37.850 --> 01:16:40.170
Beet vodka, absolute surprise.
甜菜伏特加，绝对是个惊喜。

1801
01:16:40.170 --> 01:16:42.810
And this one, not as bad as it sounds.
还有这一杯，没听起来那么糟。

1802
01:16:43.070 --> 01:16:44.390
Not as bad as it looks.
没看起来那么糟。

1803
01:16:44.390 --> 01:16:45.710
I'm not going to order it.
我可不会点这个。

1804
01:16:45.870 --> 01:16:49.650
Like, I would maybe order a scotch and Splenda.
比如，我可能会点杯苏格兰威士忌加代糖。

1805
01:16:49.830 --> 01:16:52.550
The look of it is so foul.
它看起来太恶心了。

1806
01:16:53.610 --> 01:16:56.690
It's just foul looking, but it doesn't taste as bad.
看起来确实恶心，但喝起来没那么糟。

1807
01:16:58.010 --> 01:16:59.990
Well, Samantha, there you have it.
好了，萨曼莎，情况就是这样。

1808
01:17:01.170 --> 01:17:02.230
Can I say something?
我能说句话吗？

1809
01:17:02.690 --> 01:17:03.750
I hope so.
希望你能。

1810
01:17:03.970 --> 01:17:05.210
It's not sitting in my stomach.
它没在我的胃里翻腾。

1811
01:17:05.310 --> 01:17:06.350
I wouldn't take another drink, lady.
女士，我劝你别再喝了。

1812
01:17:07.010 --> 01:17:08.290
I would stop drinking it.
我会停止饮用。

1813
01:17:08.410 --> 01:17:09.810
It's turning on me.
它开始让我反胃了。

1814
01:17:10.050 --> 01:17:10.790
Is it really?
真的吗？

1815
01:17:11.010 --> 01:17:11.270
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

1816
01:17:11.970 --> 01:17:12.490
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

1817
01:17:12.490 --> 01:17:16.090
That one tastes more like orange juice than anything else, which is good.
这一杯喝起来更像橙汁，这倒不错。

1818
01:17:16.230 --> 01:17:19.770
You know that acid-y feeling you get in your throat after you've thrown up?
你知道那种呕吐后喉咙里酸酸的感觉吗？

1819
01:17:19.970 --> 01:17:20.630
Oh, no.
噢，别说了。

1820
01:17:20.770 --> 01:17:21.810
I'm taking a sip of water now.
我现在喝口水。

1821
01:17:21.910 --> 01:17:22.090
Yeah.
是啊。

1822
01:17:22.090 --> 01:17:23.890
I used my water glass.
我用了我的水杯。

1823
01:17:24.390 --> 01:17:26.030
I'm going to take that water.
我要喝那杯水。

1824
01:17:26.270 --> 01:17:26.630
Okay.
好的。

1825
01:17:27.310 --> 01:17:28.910
Well, fair warning.
好吧，先提醒你一下。

1826
01:17:29.150 --> 01:17:30.150
It could turn on you.
它可能会让你反胃。

1827
01:17:31.230 --> 01:17:31.910
All right.
好吧。

1828
01:17:32.450 --> 01:17:32.890
Okay.
好的。

1829
01:17:33.570 --> 01:17:34.630
I will continue.
我继续。

1830
01:17:34.930 --> 01:17:37.450
I feel like I have a little bit of heartburn all of a sudden.
我突然觉得有点烧心。

1831
01:17:37.670 --> 01:17:37.890
Yeah.
是啊。

1832
01:17:37.990 --> 01:17:40.410
Are you guys feeling the heartburn in there?
你们在那儿感觉到烧心了吗？

1833
01:17:40.730 --> 01:17:41.490
A little bit.
有一点。

1834
01:17:42.550 --> 01:17:44.270
Nothing yet, but now I'm scared.
还没感觉到，但我现在开始怕了。

1835
01:17:45.630 --> 01:17:47.650
I'm really glad we're near the end.
真庆幸我们快结束了。

1836
01:17:47.870 --> 01:17:50.750
I'm glad this didn't come earlier in the episode.
真庆幸这环节没安排在节目开头。

1837
01:17:51.990 --> 01:17:52.590
All right.
好吧。

1838
01:17:52.750 --> 01:17:54.210
I should eat a banana or something.
我应该吃根香蕉什么的。

1839
01:17:55.090 --> 01:17:56.050
Where are we?
我们现在在哪儿？

1840
01:17:56.530 --> 01:17:57.570
I can't even get God's treat.
我连上帝的恩赐都享受不到。

1841
01:17:58.370 --> 01:17:58.590
Okay.
好的。

1842
01:17:59.050 --> 01:18:00.950
We are...
我们现在是……

1843
01:18:00.950 --> 01:18:03.590
Andy is moping backstage.
安迪在后台闷闷不乐。

1844
01:18:03.890 --> 01:18:04.370
Yes.
是的。

1845
01:18:04.450 --> 01:18:05.010
That's where we are.
我们就在那儿。

1846
01:18:05.130 --> 01:18:08.810
And we're about to have that great scene that we talked about with Ed.
我们马上要看到之前提到的和埃德那场精彩的戏了。

1847
01:18:09.210 --> 01:18:11.230
I absolutely love the scene.
我超级喜欢那场戏。

1848
01:18:11.230 --> 01:18:13.550
And everyone's like, Andy, you were so great.
大家都说，安迪，你演得太棒了。

1849
01:18:13.710 --> 01:18:14.850
Come on, sing us a song.
来吧，给我们唱首歌。

1850
01:18:14.970 --> 01:18:15.610
Sing a song.
唱首歌吧。

1851
01:18:15.990 --> 01:18:17.310
And he starts to sing.
然后他开始唱了起来。

1852
01:18:17.510 --> 01:18:18.430
And sorry.
抱歉。

1853
01:18:19.010 --> 01:18:20.150
It's making me burp.
这让我直打嗝。

1854
01:18:20.910 --> 01:18:22.010
I told you.
我早跟你说了。

1855
01:18:22.270 --> 01:18:24.130
I mean, how many sips did we take?
我是说，我们到底喝了几口？

1856
01:18:24.330 --> 01:18:24.970
Like two.
大概两口吧。

1857
01:18:25.250 --> 01:18:25.650
I know.
我知道。

1858
01:18:25.650 --> 01:18:27.150
And it is immediately.
而且是立刻就反应了。

1859
01:18:27.470 --> 01:18:29.390
My body is rejecting it.
我的身体在排斥它。

1860
01:18:29.470 --> 01:18:32.850
It didn't taste bad, but my body is saying don't.
味道倒是不难喝，但我的身体在说‘别喝’。

1861
01:18:32.970 --> 01:18:35.150
My eyes said don't drink that firSt.
我的眼睛一开始就说别喝那个。

1862
01:18:35.390 --> 01:18:37.910
Visually, my eyes were like, don't put that in your body.
视觉上，我的眼睛就像在说，别把那东西喝进肚子里。

1863
01:18:38.490 --> 01:18:42.750
But now my body is never wanting me to ingest that again.
但现在我的身体再也不想让我摄入那玩意儿了。

1864
01:18:42.910 --> 01:18:44.250
I took three sips.
我喝了三口。

1865
01:18:44.370 --> 01:18:45.650
I told that third sip.
我当时就对第三口说了。

1866
01:18:45.650 --> 01:18:48.610
That is like, I feel like something's burning in my cheSt.
那种感觉，我觉得胸口有什么东西在烧。

1867
01:18:48.770 --> 01:18:48.930
Okay.
好吧。

1868
01:18:49.070 --> 01:18:49.870
I'm so sorry.
真的很抱歉。

1869
01:18:50.290 --> 01:18:51.550
I had to burp.
我刚才不得不打个嗝。

1870
01:18:51.550 --> 01:18:52.490
Who wrote that?
那是谁写的？

1871
01:18:53.610 --> 01:18:55.190
Who wrote this episode?
这集是谁写的？

1872
01:18:55.430 --> 01:18:56.370
Charlie Grandy.
查理·格兰迪。

1873
01:18:56.550 --> 01:18:56.870
Charlie.
查理。

1874
01:18:57.210 --> 01:18:58.630
What have you done to us?
你对我们做了什么？

1875
01:18:58.810 --> 01:18:59.110
Okay.
好吧。

1876
01:18:59.910 --> 01:19:02.410
Anyway, everyone gathers around.
总之，大家都聚在一起。

1877
01:19:02.790 --> 01:19:04.390
I absolutely love this.
我太喜欢这一段了。

1878
01:19:04.390 --> 01:19:11.110
Daryl starts to play Macy Gray's I Try on the piano, and Andy sings his heart out.
达里尔开始在钢琴上弹奏梅西·格雷的《I Try》，安迪深情地唱了起来。

1879
01:19:11.310 --> 01:19:17.030
I went to the shooting draft, Jenna, because I wanted to see if it mentioned the Celine Dion song that Randy told us about.
珍娜，我查了拍摄剧本，因为我想看看上面有没有提到兰迪跟我们说的席琳·迪翁的那首歌。

1880
01:19:17.510 --> 01:19:18.750
It doesn't.
并没有。

1881
01:19:19.090 --> 01:19:21.030
This is what it says in the shooting draft.
拍摄剧本上是这么写的。

1882
01:19:21.390 --> 01:19:25.650
Daryl starts to play I Would Do Anything for Love by Meatloaf.
达里尔开始弹奏肉块合唱团的《I Would Do Anything for Love》。

1883
01:19:25.730 --> 01:19:26.550
Oh, my goodness.
天哪。

1884
01:19:26.990 --> 01:19:30.350
And Andy starts to sing, and I would do anything for love.
然后安迪开始唱，‘为了爱，我什么都愿意做’。

1885
01:19:30.350 --> 01:19:32.170
I'd run right into hell and back.
‘我愿冲进地狱再折返’。

1886
01:19:32.170 --> 01:19:33.910
I would do anything for love.
‘为了爱，我什么都愿意做’。

1887
01:19:34.050 --> 01:19:36.630
I'll never lie to you, and that's a fact.
‘我绝不会对你撒谎，这是事实’。

1888
01:19:37.290 --> 01:19:40.730
As Andy sings, Bob puts his arm around him.
安迪唱歌时，鲍勃搂住了他的肩膀。

1889
01:19:41.130 --> 01:19:41.730
Oh.
噢。

1890
01:19:42.050 --> 01:19:43.490
That's the shooting draft.
这就是拍摄剧本的内容。

1891
01:19:43.770 --> 01:19:54.970
Well, Randy told us that this song, Macy Gray's I Try, cost $25,000, and that Craig Robinson pre-recorded his keyboard track.
嗯，兰迪告诉我们，这首歌，也就是梅西·格雷的《I Try》，花了2.5万美元，而且克雷格·罗宾逊是预先录制好了键盘伴奏。

1892
01:19:55.110 --> 01:19:57.690
So while we're shooting, Craig is just pretending to play.
所以在拍摄时，克雷格只是假装在弹奏。

1893
01:19:57.690 --> 01:20:04.470
And the reason that they did this was so that they could keep the tempo of every take the same during editing.
他们这样做的原因是为了在剪辑时能保持每一条拍摄的节奏一致。

1894
01:20:04.670 --> 01:20:06.490
So they could cut between.
这样他们就能在不同镜头间进行剪辑。

1895
01:20:06.990 --> 01:20:15.790
The episode is going to end, we mentioned this very briefly with Ed, with my favorite tag, I think maybe ever in the series.
这一集就要结束了，我们之前和埃德简短提过，这集有我个人认为可能是全剧最棒的片尾彩蛋。

1896
01:20:15.790 --> 01:20:21.850
We are going to see Michael's audition, where he performs an entire episode of Law & Order.
我们将看到迈克尔的试镜，他表演了整整一集《法律与秩序》。

1897
01:20:22.630 --> 01:20:25.470
Including the opening and all musical interludes.
包括开场白和所有的过场音乐。

1898
01:20:25.790 --> 01:20:31.390
It starts with, in the criminal justice system, the people are defended by two separate but equally important groups.
它是这样开始的：在刑事司法系统中，人民由两支各自独立但同样重要的群体所代表。

1899
01:20:31.390 --> 01:20:35.530
The police who investigate the crimes and the district attorneys who prosecute the offenders.
一支是负责调查犯罪的警察，另一支是负责起诉罪犯的地区检察官。

1900
01:20:35.750 --> 01:20:37.130
These are their stories.
这就是他们的故事。

1901
01:20:37.310 --> 01:20:38.830
And Michael goes, kong kong!
然后迈克尔就说，咚咚！

1902
01:20:39.410 --> 01:20:44.170
Well, you know my love of Law & Order, so I thoroughly enjoyed Michael's whole monologue.
嗯，你知道我有多爱《法律与秩序》，所以我非常享受迈克尔的整段独白。

1903
01:20:44.350 --> 01:20:45.670
I needed it to go on.
我希望它能继续下去。

1904
01:20:45.790 --> 01:20:47.510
I couldn't get enough of it.
我怎么看都看不够。

1905
01:20:47.590 --> 01:20:48.870
I could not get enough of it.
我真是百看不厌。

1906
01:20:48.950 --> 01:20:50.290
I went to deleted scenes.
我甚至去看了删减片段。

1907
01:20:50.530 --> 01:20:52.090
I wanted to know if there was more.
我想知道还有没有更多内容。

1908
01:20:52.470 --> 01:20:54.330
Unfortunately, I couldn't find any other footage.
遗憾的是，我没能找到其他素材。

1909
01:20:54.530 --> 01:20:56.470
This is an email to Dave Rogers, I think.
我想这是一封发给戴夫·罗杰斯的邮件。

1910
01:20:56.630 --> 01:20:58.470
He is the holder of all footage.
他掌握着所有的拍摄素材。

1911
01:20:58.770 --> 01:21:00.190
It is absolutely brilliant.
这简直太精彩了。

1912
01:21:00.390 --> 01:21:02.370
Every single second of it is magic.
每一秒都是魔法。

1913
01:21:02.970 --> 01:21:05.850
And you guys, that was Andy's play.
还有各位，那是安迪的表演。

1914
01:21:05.850 --> 01:21:10.950
Yes, and a big thank you to Ed Helms, who joined us in studio today.
是的，非常感谢今天来到演播室的艾德·赫尔姆斯。

1915
01:21:11.290 --> 01:21:14.910
You can catch Ed's series, Rutherford Falls, on Peacock.
大家可以在Peacock平台上观看艾德的剧集《拉瑟福德的瀑布》。

1916
01:21:15.030 --> 01:21:15.770
It's wonderful.
非常棒。

1917
01:21:15.770 --> 01:21:17.010
Ed, we love you.
艾德，我们爱你。

1918
01:21:17.210 --> 01:21:20.450
And thank you to Randy Cordray for such great behind-the-scenes details.
也感谢兰迪·科德雷分享了这么多精彩的幕后细节。

1919
01:21:20.690 --> 01:21:26.950
And now, here is Ed Helms, as Andy, singing My Heart Will Go On by Celine Dion.
现在，请欣赏艾德·赫尔姆斯饰演的安迪演唱席琳·迪翁的《我心永恒》。

1920
01:21:31.560 --> 01:21:40.540
Every night in my dreams, I see you, I feel you.
每一个夜晚，在梦里，我看见你，我感觉到你。

1921
01:21:41.120 --> 01:21:46.320
That is how I know you go on.
所以我知道你依然存在。

1922
01:21:49.680 --> 01:22:03.840
Far across the distance and spaces between us, you have come to show you go on.
跨越遥远的距离和我们之间的空间，你来到这里证明你依然存在。

1923
01:22:18.050 --> 01:22:20.770
My heart does go on.
我的心确实永恒。

1924
01:22:29.800 --> 01:22:34.100
Open the door, and you're here.
打开门，你就在这里。

1925
01:22:37.420 --> 01:22:40.200
My heart will go on.
我的心将永恒。

1926
01:22:46.470 --> 01:22:54.210
Love can touch us one time, and last for a lifetime.
爱能触动我们一次，并持续一生。

1927
01:22:54.210 --> 01:23:00.290
And never let go till we're gone.
直到我们离去，永不放手。

1928
01:23:02.970 --> 01:23:07.190
Love was when I loved you.
爱曾是我爱你的时刻。

1929
01:23:08.200 --> 01:23:12.610
One true time I hold you.
我拥抱你的那唯一真切时刻。

1930
01:23:13.050 --> 01:23:17.470
And in my life, we'll always go on.
在我的一生中，我们将永远继续。

1931
01:23:20.060 --> 01:23:24.040
Paparaita-duro-o-nir far.
帕帕莱塔-杜罗-奥-尼尔法。

1932
01:23:31.960 --> 01:23:35.260
The heart does go on.
心确实永恒。

1933
01:23:36.080 --> 01:23:37.080
Yes, it does.
是的，确实如此。

1934
01:23:38.980 --> 01:23:53.030
Oh, my heart will.
噢，我的心会永恒。

1935
01:24:04.600 --> 01:24:38.410
There's no hand on.
没有手在上面。

1936
01:24:58.360 --> 01:25:00.040
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies.
感谢收听《办公室女士》。

